INSERT INTO sat_questions (question_id, external_id, vault_id, disclosed_item_id, source, program, test_type, test_type_desc, domain, primary_class_cd, skill_cd, skill_desc, difficulty, score_band_range_cd, question_type, stimulus_html, stem_html, answer_options, correct_answer, answer_keys, rationale_html, correct_answer_extracted_from_rationale, image_count, parent_template_name, parent_template_id, template_cluster_id, template_cluster_name, origin, position, answer_style, section, raw_payload, created_date, updated_date) VALUES
    ($SATQ$757077f9$SATQ$, $SATQ$c9491ece-56aa-412b-b7e3-e714bff85f82$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$c0772bf5-4bfa-4ad8-a5c5-473653e59dca$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>During a 2014 archaeological dig in Spain, Vicente Lull and his team uncovered the skeleton of a woman from El Algar, an Early Bronze Age society, buried with valuable objects signaling a high position of power. This finding may persuade researchers who have argued that Bronze Age societies were ruled by men to <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> that women may have also held leadership roles.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"70507bb8-3a3d-4da3-9dbb-784a36dd3f19","content":"<p>waive</p>"},{"id":"805479a3-2278-4019-968d-26c91fff7c62","content":"<p>concede</p>"},{"id":"6b930edd-4515-4911-8cba-dcdd93dfc0ab","content":"<p>refute</p>"},{"id":"a2b30d08-36fb-4975-a0fa-96453760392b","content":"<p>require</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["805479a3-2278-4019-968d-26c91fff7c62"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the significance of the 2014 archaeological finding at El Algar. In this context, &ldquo;concede&rdquo; means to admit something is true after first resisting that admission. The text indicates that some researchers believe &ldquo;Bronze Age societies were ruled by men.&rdquo; But the Bronze Age burial of a woman at El Algar included &ldquo;valuable objects signaling a high position of power,&rdquo; which would raise the possibility that &ldquo;women may have also held leadership roles.&rdquo; Thus, the text is calling into question the notion that only men were leaders in these societies and speculating that people holding this view may reconsider their opinion. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;waive&rdquo; means to refrain from insisting that something, such as a right or a requirement, be observed; the word isn&rsquo;t used, however, in contexts where someone acknowledges that an opinion they hold may be invalid, as is the case in the text.&nbsp;Choice C is incorrect. According to the text, the finding from the El Algar burial site undermines the view that Bronze Age societies were exclusively ruled by men. However, &ldquo;refute&rdquo; means to demonstrate that something is false and would not make sense in context. Lull and team&rsquo;s finding supports the view that women may have also held leadership roles, not that they did not participate in such roles. Choice D is incorrect because in this context, &ldquo;require&rdquo; means to demand or specify as mandatory. However, it would not make sense for contemporary researchers to demand that Bronze Age &ldquo;women may have also held leadership roles.&rdquo; </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-947-WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$c50852d6-833a-4ace-a3cf-9f234ffef0af$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"757077f9","external_id":"c9491ece-56aa-412b-b7e3-e714bff85f82","vaultid":"c0772bf5-4bfa-4ad8-a5c5-473653e59dca","uId":"0891f2cf-41c4-47df-bd6e-7d390cd528fd","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>During a 2014 archaeological dig in Spain, Vicente Lull and his team uncovered the skeleton of a woman from El Algar, an Early Bronze Age society, buried with valuable objects signaling a high position of power. This finding may persuade researchers who have argued that Bronze Age societies were ruled by men to <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> that women may have also held leadership roles.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"70507bb8-3a3d-4da3-9dbb-784a36dd3f19","content":"<p>waive</p>"},{"id":"805479a3-2278-4019-968d-26c91fff7c62","content":"<p>concede</p>"},{"id":"6b930edd-4515-4911-8cba-dcdd93dfc0ab","content":"<p>refute</p>"},{"id":"a2b30d08-36fb-4975-a0fa-96453760392b","content":"<p>require</p>"}],"keys":["805479a3-2278-4019-968d-26c91fff7c62"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the significance of the 2014 archaeological finding at El Algar. In this context, &ldquo;concede&rdquo; means to admit something is true after first resisting that admission. The text indicates that some researchers believe &ldquo;Bronze Age societies were ruled by men.&rdquo; But the Bronze Age burial of a woman at El Algar included &ldquo;valuable objects signaling a high position of power,&rdquo; which would raise the possibility that &ldquo;women may have also held leadership roles.&rdquo; Thus, the text is calling into question the notion that only men were leaders in these societies and speculating that people holding this view may reconsider their opinion. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;waive&rdquo; means to refrain from insisting that something, such as a right or a requirement, be observed; the word isn&rsquo;t used, however, in contexts where someone acknowledges that an opinion they hold may be invalid, as is the case in the text.&nbsp;Choice C is incorrect. According to the text, the finding from the El Algar burial site undermines the view that Bronze Age societies were exclusively ruled by men. However, &ldquo;refute&rdquo; means to demonstrate that something is false and would not make sense in context. Lull and team&rsquo;s finding supports the view that women may have also held leadership roles, not that they did not participate in such roles. Choice D is incorrect because in this context, &ldquo;require&rdquo; means to demand or specify as mandatory. However, it would not make sense for contemporary researchers to demand that Bronze Age &ldquo;women may have also held leadership roles.&rdquo; </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-947-WIC","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"c50852d6-833a-4ace-a3cf-9f234ffef0af","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959356,"updateDate":1691007959356}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959356, 1691007959356),
    ($SATQ$760ee1db$SATQ$, $SATQ$cd212f17-eef7-4563-b4e3-9ba6e374a6ef$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$a587b66c-cefd-4645-8083-ab7c94803fb9$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Although the playwrights hoped that their play would be <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> when performed live, critics generally agreed that the production and performances had the opposite effect, wearying audiences instead of energizing them.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"d58eb469-e4b1-43ed-9e4f-983342f4bd93","content":"<p>multifaceted</p>"},{"id":"241cd2fc-b44f-4e79-aee6-b62f89f5b59b","content":"<p>realistic</p>"},{"id":"c3b38992-dd35-4452-a857-198eeaf5f952","content":"<p>rousing</p>"},{"id":"b5c0be34-8027-4bd2-a24d-0dd218792eb8","content":"<p>subtle</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["c3b38992-dd35-4452-a857-198eeaf5f952"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the play&rsquo;s effect on audiences. As used in this context, &ldquo;rousing&rdquo; means exciting or energizing. The text indicates that critics found the play to have &ldquo;the opposite effect&rdquo; on audiences of what the playwrights hoped for. The critics, the text says, thought the play was wearying rather than energizing to viewers. This context supports the idea that the playwrights hoped live performances of the play would be energizing, or rousing, to audiences. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because there&rsquo;s no information in the text suggesting that the playwrights hoped live performances of the play would be &ldquo;multifaceted,&rdquo; or be varied or have many aspects. The text indicates that critics found the play to be wearying to audiences and that this was the opposite of what the playwrights hoped for. Multifaceted is not the opposite of wearying, but rousing is, which suggests that the playwrights hoped the play would be rousing.&nbsp;Choice B is incorrect because there&rsquo;s no information in the text suggesting that the playwrights hoped live performances of the play would be &ldquo;realistic,&rdquo; or lifelike or sensible. The text says that critics found the play to be wearying to audiences and that this was the opposite of what the playwrights hoped for. Realistic is not the opposite of wearying, but rousing is, which suggests that the playwrights hoped the play would be rousing.&nbsp;Choice D is incorrect because there&rsquo;s no information in the text suggesting that the playwrights hoped live performances of the play would be subtle, or complex or understated. The text says that critics found the play to be wearying to audiences and that this was the opposite of what the playwrights hoped for. Subtle is not the opposite of wearying, but rousing is, which suggests that the playwrights hoped the play would be rousing.&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-974-WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$f4e72d54-cea8-4f9f-8f20-a85f27b6ab94$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"760ee1db","external_id":"cd212f17-eef7-4563-b4e3-9ba6e374a6ef","vaultid":"a587b66c-cefd-4645-8083-ab7c94803fb9","uId":"7dfd3a94-5d30-4a15-93a9-9cbb544a7847","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Although the playwrights hoped that their play would be <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> when performed live, critics generally agreed that the production and performances had the opposite effect, wearying audiences instead of energizing them.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"d58eb469-e4b1-43ed-9e4f-983342f4bd93","content":"<p>multifaceted</p>"},{"id":"241cd2fc-b44f-4e79-aee6-b62f89f5b59b","content":"<p>realistic</p>"},{"id":"c3b38992-dd35-4452-a857-198eeaf5f952","content":"<p>rousing</p>"},{"id":"b5c0be34-8027-4bd2-a24d-0dd218792eb8","content":"<p>subtle</p>"}],"keys":["c3b38992-dd35-4452-a857-198eeaf5f952"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the play&rsquo;s effect on audiences. As used in this context, &ldquo;rousing&rdquo; means exciting or energizing. The text indicates that critics found the play to have &ldquo;the opposite effect&rdquo; on audiences of what the playwrights hoped for. The critics, the text says, thought the play was wearying rather than energizing to viewers. This context supports the idea that the playwrights hoped live performances of the play would be energizing, or rousing, to audiences. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because there&rsquo;s no information in the text suggesting that the playwrights hoped live performances of the play would be &ldquo;multifaceted,&rdquo; or be varied or have many aspects. The text indicates that critics found the play to be wearying to audiences and that this was the opposite of what the playwrights hoped for. Multifaceted is not the opposite of wearying, but rousing is, which suggests that the playwrights hoped the play would be rousing.&nbsp;Choice B is incorrect because there&rsquo;s no information in the text suggesting that the playwrights hoped live performances of the play would be &ldquo;realistic,&rdquo; or lifelike or sensible. The text says that critics found the play to be wearying to audiences and that this was the opposite of what the playwrights hoped for. Realistic is not the opposite of wearying, but rousing is, which suggests that the playwrights hoped the play would be rousing.&nbsp;Choice D is incorrect because there&rsquo;s no information in the text suggesting that the playwrights hoped live performances of the play would be subtle, or complex or understated. The text says that critics found the play to be wearying to audiences and that this was the opposite of what the playwrights hoped for. Subtle is not the opposite of wearying, but rousing is, which suggests that the playwrights hoped the play would be rousing.&nbsp;</p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-974-WIC","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"f4e72d54-cea8-4f9f-8f20-a85f27b6ab94","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959357,"updateDate":1691007959357}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959357, 1691007959357),
    ($SATQ$764331f8$SATQ$, $SATQ$9d1565a3-0eb4-4cce-b44b-80c836044876$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$TSP$SATQ$, $SATQ$Text Structure and Purpose$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The following text is from Louise Erdrich&rsquo;s 1986 novel <em>The Beet Queen</em>. The narrator discusses her relationship with her young niece, Dot. Celestine, the narrator&rsquo;s sister-in-law, is Dot&rsquo;s mother.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Dot was as impatient with babyhood as I. She tried at once to grow out of it. Celestine never saw that, because she, and only she, took pleasure in Dot&rsquo;s helpless softness. Only Celestine was saddened by her daughter&rsquo;s fierce progress. Day by day, Dot grew stronger. <span style="text-decoration: underline;" role="region" aria-label="Referenced Content">In her shopping-cart stroller she exercised to exhaustion, bouncing for hours to develop her leg muscles.</span></p>
</blockquote>
<p style="text-align: right;"><span class="dap_copyright">&copy;1986 by Louise Erdrich</span></p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"c7ecd5a8-b8ee-495d-aae6-d4317716ca13","content":"<p>It offers a detail that shows how Dot is growing stronger.</p>"},{"id":"067a9f75-f9fc-4a48-854e-bcc98c2dcd76","content":"<p>It expresses hope that Celestine will mature psychologically.</p>"},{"id":"8f92d14b-756b-41dc-93aa-38621183fa6c","content":"<p>It explores some of the narrator&rsquo;s psychological characteristics.</p>"},{"id":"edaa9f59-6973-48c2-bb36-a2a2d1c3c2df","content":"<p>It indicates how sad Celestine is by describing a behavior she engages in.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["c7ecd5a8-b8ee-495d-aae6-d4317716ca13"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer because it most accurately describes how the underlined sentence functions in the text as a whole. In the text, the narrator makes observations about her young niece, Dot, noting that Dot is making progress toward outgrowing babyhood and is growing stronger "day by day." The description of Dot purposefully exercising by "bouncing for hours" reinforces the narrator&rsquo;s earlier characterization of Dot. The underlined sentence thus offers a detail that shows how Dot is growing stronger.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. While a sentence earlier in the text mentions Celestine&rsquo;s psychological state (sadness because Dot is growing fast), the underlined sentence doesn&rsquo;t focus on Celestine at all. Instead, the sentence focuses on Dot&rsquo;s physical activities to show that she is getting stronger. Choice C is incorrect because the underlined sentence describes Dot&rsquo;s behavior, not the narrator&rsquo;s psychological characteristics. While a sentence earlier in the text establishes that the narrator, like Dot, was "impatient with babyhood," the underlined sentence specifically addresses Dot&rsquo;s physical activities in her stroller. Choice D is incorrect. While an earlier sentence in the text mentions that Celestine is sad, the underlined sentence doesn&rsquo;t focus on how Celestine feels nor does it describe a behavior that Celestine engages in. The sentence focuses entirely on Dot&rsquo;s actions, describing her as  "bouncing for hours" to show that she is growing stronger.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"764331f8","external_id":"9d1565a3-0eb4-4cce-b44b-80c836044876","vaultid":null,"uId":"f12a997a-31ff-47d9-a5ec-a9dfe7c771a3","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"TSP","skill_desc":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>The following text is from Louise Erdrich&rsquo;s 1986 novel <em>The Beet Queen</em>. The narrator discusses her relationship with her young niece, Dot. Celestine, the narrator&rsquo;s sister-in-law, is Dot&rsquo;s mother.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Dot was as impatient with babyhood as I. She tried at once to grow out of it. Celestine never saw that, because she, and only she, took pleasure in Dot&rsquo;s helpless softness. Only Celestine was saddened by her daughter&rsquo;s fierce progress. Day by day, Dot grew stronger. <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Referenced Content\">In her shopping-cart stroller she exercised to exhaustion, bouncing for hours to develop her leg muscles.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p style=\"text-align: right;\"><span class=\"dap_copyright\">&copy;1986 by Louise Erdrich</span></p>","stem":"<p>Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"c7ecd5a8-b8ee-495d-aae6-d4317716ca13","content":"<p>It offers a detail that shows how Dot is growing stronger.</p>"},{"id":"067a9f75-f9fc-4a48-854e-bcc98c2dcd76","content":"<p>It expresses hope that Celestine will mature psychologically.</p>"},{"id":"8f92d14b-756b-41dc-93aa-38621183fa6c","content":"<p>It explores some of the narrator&rsquo;s psychological characteristics.</p>"},{"id":"edaa9f59-6973-48c2-bb36-a2a2d1c3c2df","content":"<p>It indicates how sad Celestine is by describing a behavior she engages in.</p>"}],"keys":["c7ecd5a8-b8ee-495d-aae6-d4317716ca13"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer because it most accurately describes how the underlined sentence functions in the text as a whole. In the text, the narrator makes observations about her young niece, Dot, noting that Dot is making progress toward outgrowing babyhood and is growing stronger \"day by day.\" The description of Dot purposefully exercising by \"bouncing for hours\" reinforces the narrator&rsquo;s earlier characterization of Dot. The underlined sentence thus offers a detail that shows how Dot is growing stronger.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. While a sentence earlier in the text mentions Celestine&rsquo;s psychological state (sadness because Dot is growing fast), the underlined sentence doesn&rsquo;t focus on Celestine at all. Instead, the sentence focuses on Dot&rsquo;s physical activities to show that she is getting stronger. Choice C is incorrect because the underlined sentence describes Dot&rsquo;s behavior, not the narrator&rsquo;s psychological characteristics. While a sentence earlier in the text establishes that the narrator, like Dot, was \"impatient with babyhood,\" the underlined sentence specifically addresses Dot&rsquo;s physical activities in her stroller. Choice D is incorrect. While an earlier sentence in the text mentions that Celestine is sad, the underlined sentence doesn&rsquo;t focus on how Celestine feels nor does it describe a behavior that Celestine engages in. The sentence focuses entirely on Dot&rsquo;s actions, describing her as  \"bouncing for hours\" to show that she is growing stronger.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1755117061190,"updateDate":1755117061190}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117061190, 1755117061190),
    ($SATQ$76e4c51d$SATQ$, $SATQ$2085ab1c-d19c-4090-ba16-7c45610503e7$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$05af8b9d-adde-445a-8b58-edbc0d94ded1$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The g&uuml;iro, a musical instrument traditionally made from a dried and hollowed gourd, is thought to have originated with the Ta&iacute;no people of Puerto Rico. Players use a wooden stick to scrape along ridges cut into the side of the gourd, creating sounds that are highly <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span>: the sounds produced by g&uuml;iros can differ based on the distance between the ridges, the types of strokes the player uses, and the thickness of the gourd.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"690f1ed8-88e8-438c-b03c-815dd6867799","content":"<p>overlooked</p>"},{"id":"f311667d-a37f-473c-b18b-7da75b28a11e","content":"<p>powerful</p>"},{"id":"6a15daad-e62b-45cc-9194-33321c860f47","content":"<p>routine</p>"},{"id":"5b592df3-daf8-48de-b005-cbded88d4d88","content":"<p>variable</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["5b592df3-daf8-48de-b005-cbded88d4d88"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the sounds made by g&uuml;iros. In this context, &ldquo;variable&rdquo; means able to change. The text begins by explaining that g&uuml;iros are instruments made out of hollowed gourds with ridges cut into their sides and that players scrape the ridges with wooden sticks to produce sounds. The text goes on to say that g&uuml;iros&rsquo; sounds can change depending on gourd thickness, the distance between ridges, and the types of strokes the player uses, thus supporting the idea that the sounds created by these instruments are variable. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;overlooked&rdquo; means not being seen or noticed, and there is nothing in the text to suggest that the sounds produced by g&uuml;iros are overlooked or not noticed. Choice B is incorrect because in this context, &ldquo;powerful&rdquo; would mean having a great ability to produce an effect. While it&rsquo;s possible that the sounds produced by g&uuml;iros have a strong effect on listeners, the text doesn&rsquo;t discuss this aspect of their sounds. Choice C is incorrect because &ldquo;routine&rdquo; means usual and unvarying, and there is nothing in the text to suggest that the sounds produced by g&uuml;iros are unvarying. In fact, the text describes how the sounds produced by g&uuml;iros can differ based on several factors.&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-026-WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$36b681e9-a791-4269-9e2e-1924cdd38628$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"76e4c51d","external_id":"2085ab1c-d19c-4090-ba16-7c45610503e7","vaultid":"05af8b9d-adde-445a-8b58-edbc0d94ded1","uId":"33d4be85-e345-4668-b9b0-d4905f7d27e5","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>The g&uuml;iro, a musical instrument traditionally made from a dried and hollowed gourd, is thought to have originated with the Ta&iacute;no people of Puerto Rico. Players use a wooden stick to scrape along ridges cut into the side of the gourd, creating sounds that are highly <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span>: the sounds produced by g&uuml;iros can differ based on the distance between the ridges, the types of strokes the player uses, and the thickness of the gourd.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"690f1ed8-88e8-438c-b03c-815dd6867799","content":"<p>overlooked</p>"},{"id":"f311667d-a37f-473c-b18b-7da75b28a11e","content":"<p>powerful</p>"},{"id":"6a15daad-e62b-45cc-9194-33321c860f47","content":"<p>routine</p>"},{"id":"5b592df3-daf8-48de-b005-cbded88d4d88","content":"<p>variable</p>"}],"keys":["5b592df3-daf8-48de-b005-cbded88d4d88"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the sounds made by g&uuml;iros. In this context, &ldquo;variable&rdquo; means able to change. The text begins by explaining that g&uuml;iros are instruments made out of hollowed gourds with ridges cut into their sides and that players scrape the ridges with wooden sticks to produce sounds. The text goes on to say that g&uuml;iros&rsquo; sounds can change depending on gourd thickness, the distance between ridges, and the types of strokes the player uses, thus supporting the idea that the sounds created by these instruments are variable. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because &ldquo;overlooked&rdquo; means not being seen or noticed, and there is nothing in the text to suggest that the sounds produced by g&uuml;iros are overlooked or not noticed. Choice B is incorrect because in this context, &ldquo;powerful&rdquo; would mean having a great ability to produce an effect. While it&rsquo;s possible that the sounds produced by g&uuml;iros have a strong effect on listeners, the text doesn&rsquo;t discuss this aspect of their sounds. Choice C is incorrect because &ldquo;routine&rdquo; means usual and unvarying, and there is nothing in the text to suggest that the sounds produced by g&uuml;iros are unvarying. In fact, the text describes how the sounds produced by g&uuml;iros can differ based on several factors.&nbsp;</p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-026-WIC","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"36b681e9-a791-4269-9e2e-1924cdd38628","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959318,"updateDate":1691007959318}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959318, 1691007959318),
    ($SATQ$79dec1e1$SATQ$, $SATQ$59d4e01c-ca0e-46e7-8e34-fa003898eec8$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Art scholars have noted that some colors seem to be more <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> viewers than others. For example, people tend to find paintings featuring blues and greens more appealing than paintings featuring yellows and oranges. &nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"423b23ba-4d3a-479b-8e5c-364b371596eb","content":"<p>confusing for</p>"},{"id":"d2a41bb1-481b-4832-aa98-3a5b498bb286","content":"<p>attractive to</p>"},{"id":"910e77c4-63a5-4e9d-94e8-467a1cf57fbb","content":"<p>corrected by</p>"},{"id":"819d3e40-9c91-4582-8f3b-fac21a56a2e6","content":"<p>similar to</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["d2a41bb1-481b-4832-aa98-3a5b498bb286"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer because it best completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of how viewers respond to colors. The text presents something art scholars have noted and gives the example of people tending to find paintings with blues and greens more appealing than those with yellows and oranges. This context conveys that certain colors are more "attractive to" viewers than other colors are.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the text indicates only that people tend to find some colors more appealing than others and gives no indication that certain colors are ever "confusing for," or puzzling to, viewers. Choice C is incorrect because the text discusses the relative appeal of certain colors in paintings but gives no indication that any colors would ever be "corrected by" viewers, or somehow fixed or improved by them. Choice D is incorrect because it wouldn&rsquo;t make much sense to say that some colors are more "similar to" viewers than others, which would suggest that colors and viewers are alike to different degrees. Further, the text primarily emphasizes a difference, not a similarity, in how appealing paintings tend to be based on the colors they contain.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"79dec1e1","external_id":"59d4e01c-ca0e-46e7-8e34-fa003898eec8","vaultid":null,"uId":"8618dbc9-7635-47a8-aa47-881a3bf95e6d","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Art scholars have noted that some colors seem to be more <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> viewers than others. For example, people tend to find paintings featuring blues and greens more appealing than paintings featuring yellows and oranges. &nbsp;</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"423b23ba-4d3a-479b-8e5c-364b371596eb","content":"<p>confusing for</p>"},{"id":"d2a41bb1-481b-4832-aa98-3a5b498bb286","content":"<p>attractive to</p>"},{"id":"910e77c4-63a5-4e9d-94e8-467a1cf57fbb","content":"<p>corrected by</p>"},{"id":"819d3e40-9c91-4582-8f3b-fac21a56a2e6","content":"<p>similar to</p>"}],"keys":["d2a41bb1-481b-4832-aa98-3a5b498bb286"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer because it best completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of how viewers respond to colors. The text presents something art scholars have noted and gives the example of people tending to find paintings with blues and greens more appealing than those with yellows and oranges. This context conveys that certain colors are more \"attractive to\" viewers than other colors are.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the text indicates only that people tend to find some colors more appealing than others and gives no indication that certain colors are ever \"confusing for,\" or puzzling to, viewers. Choice C is incorrect because the text discusses the relative appeal of certain colors in paintings but gives no indication that any colors would ever be \"corrected by\" viewers, or somehow fixed or improved by them. Choice D is incorrect because it wouldn&rsquo;t make much sense to say that some colors are more \"similar to\" viewers than others, which would suggest that colors and viewers are alike to different degrees. Further, the text primarily emphasizes a difference, not a similarity, in how appealing paintings tend to be based on the colors they contain.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1743430669207,"updateDate":1743430669207}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430669207, 1743430669207),
    ($SATQ$79fe7550$SATQ$, $SATQ$48f58e5b-56ce-4765-8efd-ee56f9003796$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$0484a5ba-18e1-4166-ab13-1e39e610de94$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Researcher Haesung Jung led a 2020 study showing that individual acts of kindness can <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> prosocial behavior across a larger group. Jung and her team found that bystanders who witness a helpful act become more likely to offer help to someone else, and in doing so, can inspire still others to act.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"b78498fd-ff93-4842-aedc-b67ee4f840af","content":"<p>require</p>"},{"id":"f6282eee-f279-4b52-af3d-60852ab7e9c6","content":"<p>remember</p>"},{"id":"f4690fe4-ed34-4943-97e5-cca5279b3980","content":"<p>foster</p>"},{"id":"0d715e68-92de-4083-934a-25dc451b74a0","content":"<p>discourage</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["f4690fe4-ed34-4943-97e5-cca5279b3980"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of Jung and her team&rsquo;s study of acts of kindness. In this context, &ldquo;foster&rdquo; means encourage or promote the development of. The text indicates that Jung and her team found that seeing a helpful (or prosocial) act makes a bystander more likely to help someone else, which can in turn inspire additional people to help others. That is, the team showed that single acts of kindness can foster additional prosocial acts across a group. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because nothing in the text suggests that Jung and her team found that single acts of kindness &ldquo;require,&rdquo; or depend on or make obligatory, broader prosocial (or helpful) behavior across a group. There&rsquo;s no suggestion in the text that individual acts of kindness can only occur if other prosocial acts have already occurred, and the text indicates only that an act of kindness <em>can </em>inspire additional helpful acts, not that it necessarily will do so. Choice B is incorrect because the text focuses on a possible direct effect of individual acts of kindness, or single helpful actions, and it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense to suggest that actions can &ldquo;remember,&rdquo; or hold a memory of, something. Choice D is incorrect because the text doesn&rsquo;t indicate that Jung and her team found that single acts of kindness can &ldquo;discourage,&rdquo; or hinder, prosocial (or helpful) behavior across a group. On the contrary, the text states that Jung and her team found that seeing a helpful act makes a bystander <em>more</em> likely to help someone else, which can in turn inspire even more people to help others. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-966-WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$b053308a-6db7-4360-8fd2-0c82fadec735$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"79fe7550","external_id":"48f58e5b-56ce-4765-8efd-ee56f9003796","vaultid":"0484a5ba-18e1-4166-ab13-1e39e610de94","uId":"aff3f9f9-150e-4c17-a193-9f158bf37d65","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Researcher Haesung Jung led a 2020 study showing that individual acts of kindness can <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> prosocial behavior across a larger group. Jung and her team found that bystanders who witness a helpful act become more likely to offer help to someone else, and in doing so, can inspire still others to act.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"b78498fd-ff93-4842-aedc-b67ee4f840af","content":"<p>require</p>"},{"id":"f6282eee-f279-4b52-af3d-60852ab7e9c6","content":"<p>remember</p>"},{"id":"f4690fe4-ed34-4943-97e5-cca5279b3980","content":"<p>foster</p>"},{"id":"0d715e68-92de-4083-934a-25dc451b74a0","content":"<p>discourage</p>"}],"keys":["f4690fe4-ed34-4943-97e5-cca5279b3980"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of Jung and her team&rsquo;s study of acts of kindness. In this context, &ldquo;foster&rdquo; means encourage or promote the development of. The text indicates that Jung and her team found that seeing a helpful (or prosocial) act makes a bystander more likely to help someone else, which can in turn inspire additional people to help others. That is, the team showed that single acts of kindness can foster additional prosocial acts across a group. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because nothing in the text suggests that Jung and her team found that single acts of kindness &ldquo;require,&rdquo; or depend on or make obligatory, broader prosocial (or helpful) behavior across a group. There&rsquo;s no suggestion in the text that individual acts of kindness can only occur if other prosocial acts have already occurred, and the text indicates only that an act of kindness <em>can </em>inspire additional helpful acts, not that it necessarily will do so. Choice B is incorrect because the text focuses on a possible direct effect of individual acts of kindness, or single helpful actions, and it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense to suggest that actions can &ldquo;remember,&rdquo; or hold a memory of, something. Choice D is incorrect because the text doesn&rsquo;t indicate that Jung and her team found that single acts of kindness can &ldquo;discourage,&rdquo; or hinder, prosocial (or helpful) behavior across a group. On the contrary, the text states that Jung and her team found that seeing a helpful act makes a bystander <em>more</em> likely to help someone else, which can in turn inspire even more people to help others. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-966-WIC","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"b053308a-6db7-4360-8fd2-0c82fadec735","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959357,"updateDate":1691007959357}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959357, 1691007959357),
    ($SATQ$7a0e31ea$SATQ$, $SATQ$25b63b9f-8c2b-42d4-aac0-ac81a6ad86e9$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$TSP$SATQ$, $SATQ$Text Structure and Purpose$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The following text is from Betty Smith&rsquo;s 1943 novel <em>A Tree Grows in Brooklyn</em>. Francie, a young girl, visits the library often.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Francie thought that all the books in the world were in that library and she had a plan about reading all the books in the world. She was reading a book a day in alphabetical order and not skipping the dry ones. She remembered that the first author had been Abbott. She had been reading a book a day for a long time now and she was still in the B&rsquo;s. Already she had read about bees and buffaloes, Bermuda vacations and Byzantine architecture. For all her enthusiasm, she had to admit that some of the B&rsquo;s had been hard going. But Francie was a reader.</p>
</blockquote>
<p style="text-align: right;"><span class="dap_copyright">&copy;1947 by Betty Smith</span></p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"56c2fc2d-b525-470a-8e10-6f049ff30a10","content":"<p>To illustrate Francie&rsquo;s enjoyment of an unusual topic</p>"},{"id":"64174b6c-8830-4837-9602-50c35d7fd02b","content":"<p>To explain why Francie prefers reading over other activities</p>"},{"id":"20b6f9b0-bf24-44ae-b2c9-f40f0823bad5","content":"<p>To portray Francie&rsquo;s determination to meet a goal</p>"},{"id":"f16ebf85-3a4e-4733-842c-b4a52657a65d","content":"<p>To describe a book that Francie greatly admires</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["20b6f9b0-bf24-44ae-b2c9-f40f0823bad5"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer because it most accurately describes the main purpose of the text, which is to portray Francie&rsquo;s determination to reach her goal of reading all the books in the world. The text indicates that to achieve this aim, Francie works systematically and persistently: she reads all the books in the library in alphabetical order and devotes much time and effort to the project, finishing one book per day over a long period of time. The text then suggests that even though she progresses slowly ("she was still in the B&rsquo;s") and that she struggled with some books ("some of the B&rsquo;s had been hard going"), she doesn&rsquo;t give up because she thinks of herself as "a reader." These details show Francie&rsquo;s resolve.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. Although the text mentions several topics (bees and buffaloes, Bermuda vacations, and Byzantine architecture) that Francie has read about, it doesn&rsquo;t indicate that any of these topics are unusual or that she especially enjoyed reading about one of these topics in particular. If anything, the text suggests that she may have found some of these topics to be dull, saying that she even read the "dry ones"&mdash;that is, the boring books&mdash;and that some of the books were "hard going," meaning they were difficult to get through. Choice B is incorrect because the text doesn&rsquo;t discuss Francie&rsquo;s involvement in other activities, only her dedication to reading. Although it&rsquo;s possible that Francie dedicates herself to reading because she prefers it to other activities, the text doesn&rsquo;t indicate whether this is the case. Choice D is incorrect. Although the text mentions one author (Abbott) whose book Francie has read as well as several topics (bees and buffaloes, Bermuda vacations, and Byzantine architecture) she has encountered, the text doesn&rsquo;t say whether Francie admires any of the books she&rsquo;s read so far. Instead, the text focuses on the time and effort she devotes to reaching her goal of reading all the books in the world&mdash;even ones she doesn&rsquo;t enjoy.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"7a0e31ea","external_id":"25b63b9f-8c2b-42d4-aac0-ac81a6ad86e9","vaultid":null,"uId":"e64cc822-9a70-4136-9e1f-ca5807590936","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"TSP","skill_desc":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>The following text is from Betty Smith&rsquo;s 1943 novel <em>A Tree Grows in Brooklyn</em>. Francie, a young girl, visits the library often.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Francie thought that all the books in the world were in that library and she had a plan about reading all the books in the world. She was reading a book a day in alphabetical order and not skipping the dry ones. She remembered that the first author had been Abbott. She had been reading a book a day for a long time now and she was still in the B&rsquo;s. Already she had read about bees and buffaloes, Bermuda vacations and Byzantine architecture. For all her enthusiasm, she had to admit that some of the B&rsquo;s had been hard going. But Francie was a reader.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p style=\"text-align: right;\"><span class=\"dap_copyright\">&copy;1947 by Betty Smith</span></p>","stem":"<p>Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"56c2fc2d-b525-470a-8e10-6f049ff30a10","content":"<p>To illustrate Francie&rsquo;s enjoyment of an unusual topic</p>"},{"id":"64174b6c-8830-4837-9602-50c35d7fd02b","content":"<p>To explain why Francie prefers reading over other activities</p>"},{"id":"20b6f9b0-bf24-44ae-b2c9-f40f0823bad5","content":"<p>To portray Francie&rsquo;s determination to meet a goal</p>"},{"id":"f16ebf85-3a4e-4733-842c-b4a52657a65d","content":"<p>To describe a book that Francie greatly admires</p>"}],"keys":["20b6f9b0-bf24-44ae-b2c9-f40f0823bad5"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer because it most accurately describes the main purpose of the text, which is to portray Francie&rsquo;s determination to reach her goal of reading all the books in the world. The text indicates that to achieve this aim, Francie works systematically and persistently: she reads all the books in the library in alphabetical order and devotes much time and effort to the project, finishing one book per day over a long period of time. The text then suggests that even though she progresses slowly (\"she was still in the B&rsquo;s\") and that she struggled with some books (\"some of the B&rsquo;s had been hard going\"), she doesn&rsquo;t give up because she thinks of herself as \"a reader.\" These details show Francie&rsquo;s resolve.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. Although the text mentions several topics (bees and buffaloes, Bermuda vacations, and Byzantine architecture) that Francie has read about, it doesn&rsquo;t indicate that any of these topics are unusual or that she especially enjoyed reading about one of these topics in particular. If anything, the text suggests that she may have found some of these topics to be dull, saying that she even read the \"dry ones\"&mdash;that is, the boring books&mdash;and that some of the books were \"hard going,\" meaning they were difficult to get through. Choice B is incorrect because the text doesn&rsquo;t discuss Francie&rsquo;s involvement in other activities, only her dedication to reading. Although it&rsquo;s possible that Francie dedicates herself to reading because she prefers it to other activities, the text doesn&rsquo;t indicate whether this is the case. Choice D is incorrect. Although the text mentions one author (Abbott) whose book Francie has read as well as several topics (bees and buffaloes, Bermuda vacations, and Byzantine architecture) she has encountered, the text doesn&rsquo;t say whether Francie admires any of the books she&rsquo;s read so far. Instead, the text focuses on the time and effort she devotes to reaching her goal of reading all the books in the world&mdash;even ones she doesn&rsquo;t enjoy.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323036,"updateDate":1730147323036}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323036, 1730147323036),
    ($SATQ$7a327791$SATQ$, $SATQ$3511c2a7-97de-4c58-8cdd-06f33e46b181$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Novelist Leon Forrest admired William Faulkner&rsquo;s writing style. Forrest&rsquo;s novel <em>Divine Days</em> contains a long passage in tribute to Faulkner that is a perfect <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> of Faulkner&rsquo;s style: anyone familiar with Faulkner&rsquo;s writing would see the resemblance.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"cadd2e5e-29f7-4631-a756-ab8d8c5f9f60","content":"<p>forgetting</p>"},{"id":"3c42c8cd-dcc0-41f6-87a2-cd6260ece672","content":"<p>rejection</p>"},{"id":"155e4662-0f1f-4e45-93e3-44fde969e026","content":"<p>imitation</p>"},{"id":"b260ea1c-014e-4ea0-b019-e1522952d83d","content":"<p>opinion</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["155e4662-0f1f-4e45-93e3-44fde969e026"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of novelist Leon Forrest&rsquo;s admiration of William Faulkner&rsquo;s writing style. In this context, "imitation" means something that resembles or reproduces something else. The text states that Forrest admired Faulkner&rsquo;s style and that anyone familiar with Faulkner&rsquo;s style would be able to see the stylistic similarities between a particular passage in Forrest&rsquo;s novel <em>Divine Days</em> and Faulkner&rsquo;s writing, a fact that supports the idea that Forrest&rsquo;s novel pays tribute to Faulkner by reproducing, or imitating, Faulkner&rsquo;s style.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because in this context, a "forgetting" would mean an instance in which something is overlooked or not remembered. The text emphasizes Forrest&rsquo;s admiration for Faulkner&rsquo;s style and the fact that Forrest&rsquo;s writing in some instances closely resembles Faulkner&rsquo;s stylistically. It therefore wouldn&rsquo;t make sense to say that in trying to pay tribute to Faulkner&rsquo;s style, Forrest failed to remember it. Choice B is incorrect because in this context, a "rejection" would mean a dismissal of something as unworthy. The text emphasizes Forrest&rsquo;s admiration for Faulkner&rsquo;s writing style, stating that parts of Forrest&rsquo;s writings indicate efforts to copy that style. It wouldn&rsquo;t make sense therefore to suggest that Forrest had rejected or dismissed Faulkner&rsquo;s style as unworthy. Choice D is incorrect because in this context, an "opinion" would mean a view or judgment. Although the text focuses on Forrest&rsquo;s admiration of Faulkner, which suggests that Forrest had formed a positive judgment of Faulkner&rsquo;s style, the word opinion wouldn&rsquo;t make sense in this sentence: the sentence doesn&rsquo;t say that the passage from Forrest&rsquo;s novel expresses his view of Faulkner&rsquo;s style; rather, it suggests that stylistically, the passage closely resembles, or imitates, Faulkner&rsquo;s writing.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"7a327791","external_id":"3511c2a7-97de-4c58-8cdd-06f33e46b181","vaultid":null,"uId":"7d2e9315-5de1-4fbf-9426-52b2f7396d97","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Novelist Leon Forrest admired William Faulkner&rsquo;s writing style. Forrest&rsquo;s novel <em>Divine Days</em> contains a long passage in tribute to Faulkner that is a perfect <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> of Faulkner&rsquo;s style: anyone familiar with Faulkner&rsquo;s writing would see the resemblance.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"cadd2e5e-29f7-4631-a756-ab8d8c5f9f60","content":"<p>forgetting</p>"},{"id":"3c42c8cd-dcc0-41f6-87a2-cd6260ece672","content":"<p>rejection</p>"},{"id":"155e4662-0f1f-4e45-93e3-44fde969e026","content":"<p>imitation</p>"},{"id":"b260ea1c-014e-4ea0-b019-e1522952d83d","content":"<p>opinion</p>"}],"keys":["155e4662-0f1f-4e45-93e3-44fde969e026"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of novelist Leon Forrest&rsquo;s admiration of William Faulkner&rsquo;s writing style. In this context, \"imitation\" means something that resembles or reproduces something else. The text states that Forrest admired Faulkner&rsquo;s style and that anyone familiar with Faulkner&rsquo;s style would be able to see the stylistic similarities between a particular passage in Forrest&rsquo;s novel <em>Divine Days</em> and Faulkner&rsquo;s writing, a fact that supports the idea that Forrest&rsquo;s novel pays tribute to Faulkner by reproducing, or imitating, Faulkner&rsquo;s style.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because in this context, a \"forgetting\" would mean an instance in which something is overlooked or not remembered. The text emphasizes Forrest&rsquo;s admiration for Faulkner&rsquo;s style and the fact that Forrest&rsquo;s writing in some instances closely resembles Faulkner&rsquo;s stylistically. It therefore wouldn&rsquo;t make sense to say that in trying to pay tribute to Faulkner&rsquo;s style, Forrest failed to remember it. Choice B is incorrect because in this context, a \"rejection\" would mean a dismissal of something as unworthy. The text emphasizes Forrest&rsquo;s admiration for Faulkner&rsquo;s writing style, stating that parts of Forrest&rsquo;s writings indicate efforts to copy that style. It wouldn&rsquo;t make sense therefore to suggest that Forrest had rejected or dismissed Faulkner&rsquo;s style as unworthy. Choice D is incorrect because in this context, an \"opinion\" would mean a view or judgment. Although the text focuses on Forrest&rsquo;s admiration of Faulkner, which suggests that Forrest had formed a positive judgment of Faulkner&rsquo;s style, the word opinion wouldn&rsquo;t make sense in this sentence: the sentence doesn&rsquo;t say that the passage from Forrest&rsquo;s novel expresses his view of Faulkner&rsquo;s style; rather, it suggests that stylistically, the passage closely resembles, or imitates, Faulkner&rsquo;s writing.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323052,"updateDate":1730147323052}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323052, 1730147323052),
    ($SATQ$7afb470b$SATQ$, $SATQ$ad86475b-ae63-4b20-9842-08121ceb3bdb$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Diadromous fish migrate between freshwater and marine biomes during their life cycle. The migration&rsquo;s obligate nature is why diadromous fish can be <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> those that are merely euryhaline (able to tolerate high salinity): the euryhaline blackchin tilapia can survive high salinity, but its life cycle does not involve relocation to a different biome, as does that of the diadromous wild salmon.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"563d8a7d-e194-486c-80ab-787b43d39b39","content":"<p>demarcated from</p>"},{"id":"1b40d4b4-e7e2-408a-8a0a-5308d6033a04","content":"<p>reconstituted as</p>"},{"id":"1800217e-2075-40a0-b209-7a75752c20d7","content":"<p>conflated with</p>"},{"id":"39d1dd40-7a90-401f-888b-792f933eea4a","content":"<p>derived from</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["563d8a7d-e194-486c-80ab-787b43d39b39"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of diadromous fish. In this context, "demarcated from" means separate or set apart from. The text indicates that diadromous fish differ from euryhaline fish in that diadromous fish "migrate between freshwater and marine biomes during their life," whereas euryhaline fish do not relocate to a different biome because they can tolerate higher salinity environments. Therefore, this context suggests that because of differences between their migration patterns, diadromous fish are distinct and can be demarcated from euryhaline fish.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. Although the text states that diadromous fish migrate and relocate, the text does not suggest that diadromous fish would be "reconstituted as," or formed again as, anything new. Only their environments change and not the fish themselves. Choice C is incorrect because the text does not suggest that diadromous fish can be "conflated with," or combined with, euryhaline fish. Instead, the text distinguishes the two types of fish by pointing out their differences with regard to migration and tolerance for salinity. Choice D is incorrect because the text indicates that based on migration habits and tolerance for salinity, diadromous fish are different from euryhaline fish; so it would not make logical sense to say that diadromous fish would be "derived from," or be an extension of or result from, euryhaline fish.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"7afb470b","external_id":"ad86475b-ae63-4b20-9842-08121ceb3bdb","vaultid":null,"uId":"c3b9ff3b-3f35-4e3f-8b52-5e1d176197f9","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Diadromous fish migrate between freshwater and marine biomes during their life cycle. The migration&rsquo;s obligate nature is why diadromous fish can be <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> those that are merely euryhaline (able to tolerate high salinity): the euryhaline blackchin tilapia can survive high salinity, but its life cycle does not involve relocation to a different biome, as does that of the diadromous wild salmon.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"563d8a7d-e194-486c-80ab-787b43d39b39","content":"<p>demarcated from</p>"},{"id":"1b40d4b4-e7e2-408a-8a0a-5308d6033a04","content":"<p>reconstituted as</p>"},{"id":"1800217e-2075-40a0-b209-7a75752c20d7","content":"<p>conflated with</p>"},{"id":"39d1dd40-7a90-401f-888b-792f933eea4a","content":"<p>derived from</p>"}],"keys":["563d8a7d-e194-486c-80ab-787b43d39b39"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of diadromous fish. In this context, \"demarcated from\" means separate or set apart from. The text indicates that diadromous fish differ from euryhaline fish in that diadromous fish \"migrate between freshwater and marine biomes during their life,\" whereas euryhaline fish do not relocate to a different biome because they can tolerate higher salinity environments. Therefore, this context suggests that because of differences between their migration patterns, diadromous fish are distinct and can be demarcated from euryhaline fish.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect. Although the text states that diadromous fish migrate and relocate, the text does not suggest that diadromous fish would be \"reconstituted as,\" or formed again as, anything new. Only their environments change and not the fish themselves. Choice C is incorrect because the text does not suggest that diadromous fish can be \"conflated with,\" or combined with, euryhaline fish. Instead, the text distinguishes the two types of fish by pointing out their differences with regard to migration and tolerance for salinity. Choice D is incorrect because the text indicates that based on migration habits and tolerance for salinity, diadromous fish are different from euryhaline fish; so it would not make logical sense to say that diadromous fish would be \"derived from,\" or be an extension of or result from, euryhaline fish.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1743430669212,"updateDate":1743430669212}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430669212, 1743430669212),
    ($SATQ$7b43c0cc$SATQ$, $SATQ$145d53b4-900a-482a-924e-63f882773a6e$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Steiger Butte Drum, a family ensemble from the Klamath Tribes of the Pacific Northwest, collaborated with composer Michael Gordon to create <em>Natural History</em>, a work featuring traditional drumming and vocals alongside an orchestra and chorus. Steiger Butte Drum&rsquo;s participation is <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> to the piece: members not only contributed to its composition but also must be included in all performances.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"109b9a28-439b-4aff-ad4f-97892a4d4780","content":"<p>tangential</p>"},{"id":"d291184c-3bab-4065-ac6c-0d7e842787eb","content":"<p>subsequent</p>"},{"id":"1440a634-d6a2-4afe-a8fb-38c5d18ccda9","content":"<p>analogous</p>"},{"id":"e3ef364d-b834-483f-9263-04038e859592","content":"<p>integral</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["e3ef364d-b834-483f-9263-04038e859592"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of Steiger Butte Drum&rsquo;s contributions to the musical work <em>Natural History</em>. In this context, &ldquo;integral&rdquo; means essential or necessary to the whole. The text states that Steiger Butte Drum not only took part in the piece&rsquo;s creation, collaborating with composer Michael Gordon on it, but also &ldquo;must be included in all performances.&rdquo; This context clearly indicates that the ensemble&rsquo;s participation is essential, or integral, to the piece, both in its creation and its performance.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because in this context, &ldquo;tangential&rdquo; would mean peripheral or of little relevance to something. The text emphasizes the importance of Steiger Butte Drum&rsquo;s involvement in both the composition and performance of <em>Natural History</em>, indicating their role is central, not tangential. Choice B is incorrect because in this context, &ldquo;subsequent&rdquo; would mean following after or coming later than something else. The text doesn&rsquo;t establish a temporal sequence where the participation of Steiger Butte Drum followed after the creation of <em>Natural History</em>; rather, it indicates that the ensemble was involved with the piece from the beginning, having worked with Michael Gordon during the creation process. Choice C is incorrect because in this context, &ldquo;analogous&rdquo; would mean similar or comparable to something else, and the text doesn&rsquo;t compare Steiger Butte Drum&rsquo;s participation in the creation and performances of <em>Natural History</em> to anything else; instead, it describes the nature and importance of the ensemble&rsquo;s involvement.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"7b43c0cc","external_id":"145d53b4-900a-482a-924e-63f882773a6e","vaultid":null,"uId":"e7ac1ee2-198e-44d2-9ca7-d922b73c65e0","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Steiger Butte Drum, a family ensemble from the Klamath Tribes of the Pacific Northwest, collaborated with composer Michael Gordon to create <em>Natural History</em>, a work featuring traditional drumming and vocals alongside an orchestra and chorus. Steiger Butte Drum&rsquo;s participation is <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> to the piece: members not only contributed to its composition but also must be included in all performances.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"109b9a28-439b-4aff-ad4f-97892a4d4780","content":"<p>tangential</p>"},{"id":"d291184c-3bab-4065-ac6c-0d7e842787eb","content":"<p>subsequent</p>"},{"id":"1440a634-d6a2-4afe-a8fb-38c5d18ccda9","content":"<p>analogous</p>"},{"id":"e3ef364d-b834-483f-9263-04038e859592","content":"<p>integral</p>"}],"keys":["e3ef364d-b834-483f-9263-04038e859592"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of Steiger Butte Drum&rsquo;s contributions to the musical work <em>Natural History</em>. In this context, &ldquo;integral&rdquo; means essential or necessary to the whole. The text states that Steiger Butte Drum not only took part in the piece&rsquo;s creation, collaborating with composer Michael Gordon on it, but also &ldquo;must be included in all performances.&rdquo; This context clearly indicates that the ensemble&rsquo;s participation is essential, or integral, to the piece, both in its creation and its performance.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because in this context, &ldquo;tangential&rdquo; would mean peripheral or of little relevance to something. The text emphasizes the importance of Steiger Butte Drum&rsquo;s involvement in both the composition and performance of <em>Natural History</em>, indicating their role is central, not tangential. Choice B is incorrect because in this context, &ldquo;subsequent&rdquo; would mean following after or coming later than something else. The text doesn&rsquo;t establish a temporal sequence where the participation of Steiger Butte Drum followed after the creation of <em>Natural History</em>; rather, it indicates that the ensemble was involved with the piece from the beginning, having worked with Michael Gordon during the creation process. Choice C is incorrect because in this context, &ldquo;analogous&rdquo; would mean similar or comparable to something else, and the text doesn&rsquo;t compare Steiger Butte Drum&rsquo;s participation in the creation and performances of <em>Natural History</em> to anything else; instead, it describes the nature and importance of the ensemble&rsquo;s involvement.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1776362771167,"updateDate":1776362771167}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1776362771167, 1776362771167),
    ($SATQ$7b4dde72$SATQ$, $SATQ$c2c803b2-12ef-43e1-9e6f-fd55ed2b943f$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>In 1891, design artist William Morris cofounded the Kelmscott Press, which printed editions of books using preindustrial methods. Historians argue that Morris&rsquo;s repudiation of industrialization is <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> the Kelmscott editions&rsquo; use of handmade materials and intricate ornamentation reminiscent of medieval manuscripts: these meticulously handcrafted elements exemplify the artistry involved.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"62574f9d-7873-4bd4-8467-9c205d65c9f2","content":"<p>insensible to</p>"},{"id":"f9664c27-7583-431f-8d28-5cb1e77977b5","content":"<p>manifest in</p>"},{"id":"af559717-00fe-42d9-9ed1-a4933d486bcf","content":"<p>scrutinized by</p>"},{"id":"9dfc4692-f8eb-4c66-bc00-9b9388213c9c","content":"<p>complicated by</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["f9664c27-7583-431f-8d28-5cb1e77977b5"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the Kelmscott Press&rsquo;s books. In this context, "manifest in" means evident or apparent from. The text states that the Kelmscott Press, which was cofounded by William Morris, produced its books using preindustrial methods. The text notes the similarity between those methods, which include the use of handmade materials and intricate ornamentation, and methods used in the creation of medieval manuscripts. This context suggests that Morris&rsquo;s repudiation of industrialization is apparent from, or manifest in, the methods and materials his company employed.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because there is nothing in the text to suggest that Morris&rsquo;s repudiation of industrialization is "insensible to," or unaware of or lacking perception of, the use of handmade materials and intricate ornamentation in the production of the Kelmscott editions. Instead, the text suggests that the methods and materials used to produce the Kelmscott editions are evidence of Morris&rsquo;s repudiation of industrialization. Choice C is incorrect because it would not make sense to say that Morris&rsquo;s repudiation of industrialization was "scrutinized by," or examined closely by, the Kelmscott editions&rsquo; use of handmade materials and intricate ornamentation. Although creating the Kelmscott editions may have involved examining the books closely, the text does not mention this aspect of Morris&rsquo;s work, and in any case, the action of using certain materials to create those editions cannot scrutinize Morris&rsquo;s attitude toward industrialization. Choice D is incorrect because the text gives no indication that Morris&rsquo;s repudiation of industrialization is "complicated by," or made more complex or difficult by, the Kelmscott Press&rsquo;s use of preindustrial methods and handcrafted elements to produce books. Instead, the text presents those methods as exemplifying Morris&rsquo;s repudiation of industrialization.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"7b4dde72","external_id":"c2c803b2-12ef-43e1-9e6f-fd55ed2b943f","vaultid":null,"uId":"98658fee-3d19-41d6-ab9f-fae3c01efa42","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>In 1891, design artist William Morris cofounded the Kelmscott Press, which printed editions of books using preindustrial methods. Historians argue that Morris&rsquo;s repudiation of industrialization is <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> the Kelmscott editions&rsquo; use of handmade materials and intricate ornamentation reminiscent of medieval manuscripts: these meticulously handcrafted elements exemplify the artistry involved.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"62574f9d-7873-4bd4-8467-9c205d65c9f2","content":"<p>insensible to</p>"},{"id":"f9664c27-7583-431f-8d28-5cb1e77977b5","content":"<p>manifest in</p>"},{"id":"af559717-00fe-42d9-9ed1-a4933d486bcf","content":"<p>scrutinized by</p>"},{"id":"9dfc4692-f8eb-4c66-bc00-9b9388213c9c","content":"<p>complicated by</p>"}],"keys":["f9664c27-7583-431f-8d28-5cb1e77977b5"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the Kelmscott Press&rsquo;s books. In this context, \"manifest in\" means evident or apparent from. The text states that the Kelmscott Press, which was cofounded by William Morris, produced its books using preindustrial methods. The text notes the similarity between those methods, which include the use of handmade materials and intricate ornamentation, and methods used in the creation of medieval manuscripts. This context suggests that Morris&rsquo;s repudiation of industrialization is apparent from, or manifest in, the methods and materials his company employed.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because there is nothing in the text to suggest that Morris&rsquo;s repudiation of industrialization is \"insensible to,\" or unaware of or lacking perception of, the use of handmade materials and intricate ornamentation in the production of the Kelmscott editions. Instead, the text suggests that the methods and materials used to produce the Kelmscott editions are evidence of Morris&rsquo;s repudiation of industrialization. Choice C is incorrect because it would not make sense to say that Morris&rsquo;s repudiation of industrialization was \"scrutinized by,\" or examined closely by, the Kelmscott editions&rsquo; use of handmade materials and intricate ornamentation. Although creating the Kelmscott editions may have involved examining the books closely, the text does not mention this aspect of Morris&rsquo;s work, and in any case, the action of using certain materials to create those editions cannot scrutinize Morris&rsquo;s attitude toward industrialization. Choice D is incorrect because the text gives no indication that Morris&rsquo;s repudiation of industrialization is \"complicated by,\" or made more complex or difficult by, the Kelmscott Press&rsquo;s use of preindustrial methods and handcrafted elements to produce books. Instead, the text presents those methods as exemplifying Morris&rsquo;s repudiation of industrialization.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323052,"updateDate":1730147323052}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323052, 1730147323052),
    ($SATQ$7b55e895$SATQ$, $SATQ$2085e5c2-ac9c-413c-aea2-aaa8e08135ac$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$f926ece7-2dac-43f0-a663-1cabddc19fc4$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$CTC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Cross-Text Connections$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p><strong>Text 1</strong></p>
<p>Some animal species, like the leopard, can be found in many kinds of areas. On the other hand, tropical mountain bird species tend to be limited in the types of spaces they can call home. This is because many mountain bird species are only able to survive at very specific elevations. Over time, these species have likely become used to living at a specific temperature. Therefore, these species struggle to survive at elevations that are warmer or colder than they are used to.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Text 2</strong></p>
<p>A new study reviewed observations of nearly 3,000 bird species to understand why tropical mountain bird species live at specific elevations. They noted that when a mountain bird species was found in an area with many other bird species, it tended to inhabit much smaller geographic areas. It is thus likely that competition for resources with other species, not temperature, limits where these birds can live.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Based on the texts, both authors would most likely agree with which statement?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"4a385ae5-195e-4c3f-89e4-a8f0ff1cdbc5","content":"<p>Tropical mountain bird species are restricted in where they can live.</p>"},{"id":"05dac10e-cd41-4db6-a5ea-2993bac4f6ab","content":"<p>Scientists have better tools to observe tropical mountain birds than they did in the past.</p>"},{"id":"8779fe45-c8b3-4cf7-9d00-676a2d76a0b3","content":"<p>Little is known about how tropical mountain birds build their nests.</p>"},{"id":"70503900-dc02-4f26-b682-1ccec49e3b1f","content":"<p>Tropical mountain bird species that live at high elevations tend to be genetically similar.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["4a385ae5-195e-4c3f-89e4-a8f0ff1cdbc5"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. Both texts state that tropical mountain bird species have limited ranges or habitats, although they disagree on the reason for this. Text 1 claims that temperature is the main factor that determines where these birds can live, while Text 2 claims that competition with other species is the main factor. However, both texts agree that these birds are not able to survive in many kinds of areas. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect. Neither text mentions the tools or methods that scientists use to observe these birds, either now or in the past. Choice C is incorrect. Neither text mentions anything about how these birds build their nests. Choice D is incorrect. Neither text provides any information about the genetic similarity of these birds, so we have no evidence that either author would agree with this statement. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-CTC-E010$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$787cdec2-659f-4280-ae46-6ccba0fbbf7d$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"7b55e895","external_id":"2085e5c2-ac9c-413c-aea2-aaa8e08135ac","vaultid":"f926ece7-2dac-43f0-a663-1cabddc19fc4","uId":"e1f739e5-7f96-4f02-89b3-cdd454d73805","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"CTC","skill_desc":"Cross-Text Connections","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p><strong>Text 1</strong></p>\n<p>Some animal species, like the leopard, can be found in many kinds of areas. On the other hand, tropical mountain bird species tend to be limited in the types of spaces they can call home. This is because many mountain bird species are only able to survive at very specific elevations. Over time, these species have likely become used to living at a specific temperature. Therefore, these species struggle to survive at elevations that are warmer or colder than they are used to.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Text 2</strong></p>\n<p>A new study reviewed observations of nearly 3,000 bird species to understand why tropical mountain bird species live at specific elevations. They noted that when a mountain bird species was found in an area with many other bird species, it tended to inhabit much smaller geographic areas. It is thus likely that competition for resources with other species, not temperature, limits where these birds can live.</p>","stem":"<p>Based on the texts, both authors would most likely agree with which statement?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"4a385ae5-195e-4c3f-89e4-a8f0ff1cdbc5","content":"<p>Tropical mountain bird species are restricted in where they can live.</p>"},{"id":"05dac10e-cd41-4db6-a5ea-2993bac4f6ab","content":"<p>Scientists have better tools to observe tropical mountain birds than they did in the past.</p>"},{"id":"8779fe45-c8b3-4cf7-9d00-676a2d76a0b3","content":"<p>Little is known about how tropical mountain birds build their nests.</p>"},{"id":"70503900-dc02-4f26-b682-1ccec49e3b1f","content":"<p>Tropical mountain bird species that live at high elevations tend to be genetically similar.</p>"}],"keys":["4a385ae5-195e-4c3f-89e4-a8f0ff1cdbc5"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is the best answer. Both texts state that tropical mountain bird species have limited ranges or habitats, although they disagree on the reason for this. Text 1 claims that temperature is the main factor that determines where these birds can live, while Text 2 claims that competition with other species is the main factor. However, both texts agree that these birds are not able to survive in many kinds of areas. </p><p>Choice B is incorrect. Neither text mentions the tools or methods that scientists use to observe these birds, either now or in the past. Choice C is incorrect. Neither text mentions anything about how these birds build their nests. Choice D is incorrect. Neither text provides any information about the genetic similarity of these birds, so we have no evidence that either author would agree with this statement. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-CTC-E010","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"787cdec2-659f-4280-ae46-6ccba0fbbf7d","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959365,"updateDate":1691007959365}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959365, 1691007959365),
    ($SATQ$7bc05fa2$SATQ$, $SATQ$cbf9da5f-f1c5-430c-b2fd-d27e74034d2f$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$fa18f335-2b61-4309-9c9d-c770edf51d2a$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Whether the reign of a French monarch such as Hugh Capet or Henry I was historically consequential or relatively uneventful, its trajectory was shaped by questions of legitimacy and therefore cannot be understood without a corollary understanding of the factors that allowed the monarch to <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> his right to hold the throne.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"7dbc58b9-5c4c-4e3b-8c8a-29197fc7455f","content":"<p>disengage</p>"},{"id":"b5786466-c908-48c5-ab7a-ece97467a690","content":"<p>annotate</p>"},{"id":"41269d30-f28f-4ffb-a9f7-3d73a7f4efa6","content":"<p>buttress</p>"},{"id":"9bcdb63b-cc34-4021-9164-d8c317b83711","content":"<p>reciprocate</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["41269d30-f28f-4ffb-a9f7-3d73a7f4efa6"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the legitimacy of the reigns of French monarchs such as Hugh Capet and Henry I. As used in this context, &ldquo;buttress&rdquo; means to strengthen or defend. The text indicates that regardless of whether a French monarch&rsquo;s reign was significant or uneventful, each monarch faced questions about his right to the throne. The text goes on to say that in order to understand the path of a French monarch&rsquo;s reign, it&rsquo;s important to understand what contributed to the monarch&rsquo;s ability to &ldquo;hold the throne.&rdquo; This context suggests that French monarchs such as Hugh Capet and Henry I had to buttress, or defend, their right to be monarch.&nbsp;</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense in context to discuss factors that enabled a monarch to &ldquo;disengage,&rdquo; or withdraw his right to the French throne. The text focuses on an examination of people who reigned as French monarchs, not on people who didn&rsquo;t choose to rule.&nbsp;Choice B is incorrect because it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense in context to discuss factors that enabled a monarch to &ldquo;annotate,&rdquo; or add notes to or explain, his right to the French throne. Nothing in the text suggests that the monarchs were writing notes about their right to the throne; instead, faced with questions about the legitimacy of their reign, the monarchs defended their right.&nbsp;Choice D is incorrect. Saying that a monarch who is faced with questions about the legitimacy of his reign was able to &ldquo;reciprocate&rdquo; his right to the French throne would mean that he either returned his right to the throne or that he responded in kind to the challenge. Neither of these meanings would make sense in context because the text focuses on people who did reign as French monarchs and defended their right to do so. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$T2007$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$f69af86d-450c-4a3a-a207-1e9ac87b2815$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"7bc05fa2","external_id":"cbf9da5f-f1c5-430c-b2fd-d27e74034d2f","vaultid":"fa18f335-2b61-4309-9c9d-c770edf51d2a","uId":"5db2f58f-2236-4844-a53c-c7e923b75f8a","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Whether the reign of a French monarch such as Hugh Capet or Henry I was historically consequential or relatively uneventful, its trajectory was shaped by questions of legitimacy and therefore cannot be understood without a corollary understanding of the factors that allowed the monarch to <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> his right to hold the throne.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"7dbc58b9-5c4c-4e3b-8c8a-29197fc7455f","content":"<p>disengage</p>"},{"id":"b5786466-c908-48c5-ab7a-ece97467a690","content":"<p>annotate</p>"},{"id":"41269d30-f28f-4ffb-a9f7-3d73a7f4efa6","content":"<p>buttress</p>"},{"id":"9bcdb63b-cc34-4021-9164-d8c317b83711","content":"<p>reciprocate</p>"}],"keys":["41269d30-f28f-4ffb-a9f7-3d73a7f4efa6"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the legitimacy of the reigns of French monarchs such as Hugh Capet and Henry I. As used in this context, &ldquo;buttress&rdquo; means to strengthen or defend. The text indicates that regardless of whether a French monarch&rsquo;s reign was significant or uneventful, each monarch faced questions about his right to the throne. The text goes on to say that in order to understand the path of a French monarch&rsquo;s reign, it&rsquo;s important to understand what contributed to the monarch&rsquo;s ability to &ldquo;hold the throne.&rdquo; This context suggests that French monarchs such as Hugh Capet and Henry I had to buttress, or defend, their right to be monarch.&nbsp;</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense in context to discuss factors that enabled a monarch to &ldquo;disengage,&rdquo; or withdraw his right to the French throne. The text focuses on an examination of people who reigned as French monarchs, not on people who didn&rsquo;t choose to rule.&nbsp;Choice B is incorrect because it wouldn&rsquo;t make sense in context to discuss factors that enabled a monarch to &ldquo;annotate,&rdquo; or add notes to or explain, his right to the French throne. Nothing in the text suggests that the monarchs were writing notes about their right to the throne; instead, faced with questions about the legitimacy of their reign, the monarchs defended their right.&nbsp;Choice D is incorrect. Saying that a monarch who is faced with questions about the legitimacy of his reign was able to &ldquo;reciprocate&rdquo; his right to the French throne would mean that he either returned his right to the throne or that he responded in kind to the challenge. Neither of these meanings would make sense in context because the text focuses on people who did reign as French monarchs and defended their right to do so. </p>","parenttemplatename":"T2007","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"f69af86d-450c-4a3a-a207-1e9ac87b2815","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959378,"updateDate":1691007959378}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959378, 1691007959378),
    ($SATQ$7bf79a90$SATQ$, $SATQ$6a5801a5-5e56-4059-a9f9-0a1240267b59$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$61dc09ce-0054-44af-8827-475dea1b43bc$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$CTC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Cross-Text Connections$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p><span role="heading" aria-level="2"><strong>Text 1</strong></span></p>
<p>Microbes are tiny organisms in the soil, water, and air all around us. They thrive even in very harsh conditions. That&rsquo;s why Noah Fierer and colleagues were surprised when soil samples they collected from an extremely cold, dry area in Antarctica didn&rsquo;t seem to contain any life. The finding doesn&rsquo;t prove that there are no microbes in that area, but the team says it does suggest that the environment severely restricts microbes&rsquo; survival.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span role="heading" aria-level="2"><strong>Text 2</strong></span></p>
<p>Microbes are found in virtually every environment on Earth. So it&rsquo;s unlikely they would be completely absent from Fierer&rsquo;s team&rsquo;s study site, no matter how extreme the environment is. There were probably so few organisms in the samples that current technology couldn&rsquo;t detect them. But since a spoonful of typical soil elsewhere might contain billions of microbes, the presence of so few in the Antarctic soil samples would show how challenging the conditions are.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Based on the texts, Fierer&rsquo;s team and the author of Text 2 would most likely agree with which statement about microbes?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"e5979a11-7c56-4aaa-92a0-51d9f36b2f2c","content":"<p>Most microbes are better able to survive in environments with extremely dry conditions than in environments with harsh temperatures.</p>"},{"id":"dfb5af88-189b-4dd8-afa7-13764b177bb4","content":"<p>A much higher number of microbes would probably be found if another sample of soil were taken from the Antarctic study site.</p>"},{"id":"e01dbb78-55ac-4f99-977a-ef7c78a1b998","content":"<p>Microbes are likely difficult to detect in the soil at the Antarctic study site because they tend to be smaller than microbes found in typical soil elsewhere.</p>"},{"id":"81624dc0-e6f5-4af0-b84b-7b922ec9b299","content":"<p>Most microbes are probably unable to withstand the soil conditions at the Antarctic study site.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["81624dc0-e6f5-4af0-b84b-7b922ec9b299"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer because it presents a statement about microbes with which Fierer&rsquo;s team (Text 1) and the author of Text 2 would most likely agree. Text 1 states that microbes usually thrive in very harsh conditions, and so Fierer&rsquo;s team was surprised when samples collected from an extremely cold and dry area of Antarctica didn&rsquo;t appear to contain any life. Fierer&rsquo;s team says that though this doesn&rsquo;t conclusively prove there are no microbes in the area, it suggests that microbes would have a notably difficult time surviving in the environment. The author of Text 2 says it&rsquo;s unlikely that there would be no microbes at all in the Antarctic study site from which Fierer&rsquo;s team retrieved soil samples and that there may have been hard-to-detect microbes in the samples. However, the presence of only a few microbes in the Antarctic samples rather than the billions found in a typical soil sample (which would presumably be much easier to detect) would illustrate conditions in the Antarctic soil that make it difficult for microbes to thrive. Since Fierer&rsquo;s team says that the seeming absence of microbes in the Antarctic samples suggests an unusually harsh environment and the author of Text 2 says that even if there are a few undetectable microbes in the samples, the relatively tiny number of microbes would also suggest an unusually harsh environment, then Fierer&rsquo;s team and the author of Text 2 would most likely agree that most microbes are unable to withstand the soil conditions at the Antarctic study site. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The samples taken by Fierer&rsquo;s team were from an area of Antarctica that is described in part as extremely dry, and these samples didn&rsquo;t appear to have any life. Therefore, even though these samples also came from an extremely cold area, Fierer&rsquo;s team wouldn&rsquo;t argue based on the evidence available that microbes were better able to survive in dry conditions than in areas with harsh temperatures. Moreover, the author of Text 2 says that microbes are found in virtually every environment on Earth but doesn&rsquo;t compare dry environments and harsh environments. Choice B is incorrect. Nothing in Text 1 indicates that another collection of samples from the Antarctic study site might yield different results from the samples already taken by Fierer&rsquo;s team. The author of Text 2 does state that microbes are found in virtually every environment on Earth and suggests that new technology may be better able to detect so few microbes in a soil sample, but the author of Text 2 concludes that the unusual absence of microbes in the Antarctic samples is evidence of the harsh Antarctic environment. Therefore, there is no reason to believe that the author of Text 2 thinks that another sample drawn from that same harsh environment would yield a much higher number of microbes. Choice C is incorrect. The author of Text 2 does speculate that there may have been so few microbes in the Antarctic samples that current technology couldn&rsquo;t detect them, but the author doesn&rsquo;t speculate that this is due to the size of the microbes. Moreover, nothing that Fierer&rsquo;s team says suggests that they are speculating that their samples might have microbes that are smaller than microbes in typical soil samples. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-014-CTC$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$dcf77a1a-cbb1-4643-b82c-56297df59a1e$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"7bf79a90","external_id":"6a5801a5-5e56-4059-a9f9-0a1240267b59","vaultid":"61dc09ce-0054-44af-8827-475dea1b43bc","uId":"26bc290c-dc09-427e-a59f-1f2e2f2f1de5","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"CTC","skill_desc":"Cross-Text Connections","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p><span role=\"heading\" aria-level=\"2\"><strong>Text 1</strong></span></p>\n<p>Microbes are tiny organisms in the soil, water, and air all around us. They thrive even in very harsh conditions. That&rsquo;s why Noah Fierer and colleagues were surprised when soil samples they collected from an extremely cold, dry area in Antarctica didn&rsquo;t seem to contain any life. The finding doesn&rsquo;t prove that there are no microbes in that area, but the team says it does suggest that the environment severely restricts microbes&rsquo; survival.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span role=\"heading\" aria-level=\"2\"><strong>Text 2</strong></span></p>\n<p>Microbes are found in virtually every environment on Earth. So it&rsquo;s unlikely they would be completely absent from Fierer&rsquo;s team&rsquo;s study site, no matter how extreme the environment is. There were probably so few organisms in the samples that current technology couldn&rsquo;t detect them. But since a spoonful of typical soil elsewhere might contain billions of microbes, the presence of so few in the Antarctic soil samples would show how challenging the conditions are.</p>","stem":"<p>Based on the texts, Fierer&rsquo;s team and the author of Text 2 would most likely agree with which statement about microbes?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"e5979a11-7c56-4aaa-92a0-51d9f36b2f2c","content":"<p>Most microbes are better able to survive in environments with extremely dry conditions than in environments with harsh temperatures.</p>"},{"id":"dfb5af88-189b-4dd8-afa7-13764b177bb4","content":"<p>A much higher number of microbes would probably be found if another sample of soil were taken from the Antarctic study site.</p>"},{"id":"e01dbb78-55ac-4f99-977a-ef7c78a1b998","content":"<p>Microbes are likely difficult to detect in the soil at the Antarctic study site because they tend to be smaller than microbes found in typical soil elsewhere.</p>"},{"id":"81624dc0-e6f5-4af0-b84b-7b922ec9b299","content":"<p>Most microbes are probably unable to withstand the soil conditions at the Antarctic study site.</p>"}],"keys":["81624dc0-e6f5-4af0-b84b-7b922ec9b299"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer because it presents a statement about microbes with which Fierer&rsquo;s team (Text 1) and the author of Text 2 would most likely agree. Text 1 states that microbes usually thrive in very harsh conditions, and so Fierer&rsquo;s team was surprised when samples collected from an extremely cold and dry area of Antarctica didn&rsquo;t appear to contain any life. Fierer&rsquo;s team says that though this doesn&rsquo;t conclusively prove there are no microbes in the area, it suggests that microbes would have a notably difficult time surviving in the environment. The author of Text 2 says it&rsquo;s unlikely that there would be no microbes at all in the Antarctic study site from which Fierer&rsquo;s team retrieved soil samples and that there may have been hard-to-detect microbes in the samples. However, the presence of only a few microbes in the Antarctic samples rather than the billions found in a typical soil sample (which would presumably be much easier to detect) would illustrate conditions in the Antarctic soil that make it difficult for microbes to thrive. Since Fierer&rsquo;s team says that the seeming absence of microbes in the Antarctic samples suggests an unusually harsh environment and the author of Text 2 says that even if there are a few undetectable microbes in the samples, the relatively tiny number of microbes would also suggest an unusually harsh environment, then Fierer&rsquo;s team and the author of Text 2 would most likely agree that most microbes are unable to withstand the soil conditions at the Antarctic study site. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The samples taken by Fierer&rsquo;s team were from an area of Antarctica that is described in part as extremely dry, and these samples didn&rsquo;t appear to have any life. Therefore, even though these samples also came from an extremely cold area, Fierer&rsquo;s team wouldn&rsquo;t argue based on the evidence available that microbes were better able to survive in dry conditions than in areas with harsh temperatures. Moreover, the author of Text 2 says that microbes are found in virtually every environment on Earth but doesn&rsquo;t compare dry environments and harsh environments. Choice B is incorrect. Nothing in Text 1 indicates that another collection of samples from the Antarctic study site might yield different results from the samples already taken by Fierer&rsquo;s team. The author of Text 2 does state that microbes are found in virtually every environment on Earth and suggests that new technology may be better able to detect so few microbes in a soil sample, but the author of Text 2 concludes that the unusual absence of microbes in the Antarctic samples is evidence of the harsh Antarctic environment. Therefore, there is no reason to believe that the author of Text 2 thinks that another sample drawn from that same harsh environment would yield a much higher number of microbes. Choice C is incorrect. The author of Text 2 does speculate that there may have been so few microbes in the Antarctic samples that current technology couldn&rsquo;t detect them, but the author doesn&rsquo;t speculate that this is due to the size of the microbes. Moreover, nothing that Fierer&rsquo;s team says suggests that they are speculating that their samples might have microbes that are smaller than microbes in typical soil samples. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-014-CTC","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"dcf77a1a-cbb1-4643-b82c-56297df59a1e","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959315,"updateDate":1691007959315}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959315, 1691007959315),
    ($SATQ$7d075fc5$SATQ$, $SATQ$3b857205-9399-406c-9581-60229257194e$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$TSP$SATQ$, $SATQ$Text Structure and Purpose$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Oral histories&mdash;whether they consist of interviews or recordings of songs and stories&mdash;can offer researchers a rich view of people&rsquo;s everyday experiences. For her book about coal mining communities in Kentucky during the twentieth century, Karida Brown therefore relied in part on interviews with coal miners and their families. <span style="text-decoration: underline;" role="region" aria-label="Referenced Content">By doing so, she gained valuable insights into her subjects&rsquo; day-to-day lives.</span></p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"3497adb6-42ef-45bf-a2fd-ffddfdb70367","content":"<p>It provides a little-known geographical fact about Kentucky.</p>"},{"id":"e4c3f183-76f6-4ce0-81b2-5d07b5278426","content":"<p>It argues that Karida Brown is an expert on United States politics.</p>"},{"id":"b5729008-f93f-49a3-97d1-def8fb566c23","content":"<p>It presents a major historical event that took place in the twentieth century.</p>"},{"id":"622f7067-eba7-465e-8f49-9ea33d54e7ba","content":"<p>It describes how Karida Brown benefited from incorporating oral history in her book.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["622f7067-eba7-465e-8f49-9ea33d54e7ba"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer because it most accurately describes how the underlined sentence functions in the text as a whole. The text begins by pointing out one of the advantages of oral histories: that they allow researchers to document the daily experiences of people. The text then goes on to describe how Karida Brown utilized interviews with coal miners and their families for her book about twentieth-century coal mining in Kentucky. The underlined sentence affirms that the general advantages of oral histories mentioned earlier in the text were also benefits in Brown&rsquo;s particular case. Thus, the underlined sentence describes how Karida Brown benefited from incorporating oral history in her book.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because though the text mentions coal miners who live in Kentucky, the underlined sentence does not offer a geographical fact about Kentucky. Choice B is incorrect because the underlined sentence does not mention United States politics or that Brown is an expert in this particular area. Choice C is incorrect. Although the text mentions that Brown&rsquo;s book revolved around coal miners during the twentieth century, the underlined sentence does not focus on a major historical event during this time.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"7d075fc5","external_id":"3b857205-9399-406c-9581-60229257194e","vaultid":null,"uId":"877f8ed3-8200-4855-bf07-0def8ec4ca65","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"TSP","skill_desc":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Oral histories&mdash;whether they consist of interviews or recordings of songs and stories&mdash;can offer researchers a rich view of people&rsquo;s everyday experiences. For her book about coal mining communities in Kentucky during the twentieth century, Karida Brown therefore relied in part on interviews with coal miners and their families. <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Referenced Content\">By doing so, she gained valuable insights into her subjects&rsquo; day-to-day lives.</span></p>","stem":"<p>Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"3497adb6-42ef-45bf-a2fd-ffddfdb70367","content":"<p>It provides a little-known geographical fact about Kentucky.</p>"},{"id":"e4c3f183-76f6-4ce0-81b2-5d07b5278426","content":"<p>It argues that Karida Brown is an expert on United States politics.</p>"},{"id":"b5729008-f93f-49a3-97d1-def8fb566c23","content":"<p>It presents a major historical event that took place in the twentieth century.</p>"},{"id":"622f7067-eba7-465e-8f49-9ea33d54e7ba","content":"<p>It describes how Karida Brown benefited from incorporating oral history in her book.</p>"}],"keys":["622f7067-eba7-465e-8f49-9ea33d54e7ba"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer because it most accurately describes how the underlined sentence functions in the text as a whole. The text begins by pointing out one of the advantages of oral histories: that they allow researchers to document the daily experiences of people. The text then goes on to describe how Karida Brown utilized interviews with coal miners and their families for her book about twentieth-century coal mining in Kentucky. The underlined sentence affirms that the general advantages of oral histories mentioned earlier in the text were also benefits in Brown&rsquo;s particular case. Thus, the underlined sentence describes how Karida Brown benefited from incorporating oral history in her book.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because though the text mentions coal miners who live in Kentucky, the underlined sentence does not offer a geographical fact about Kentucky. Choice B is incorrect because the underlined sentence does not mention United States politics or that Brown is an expert in this particular area. Choice C is incorrect. Although the text mentions that Brown&rsquo;s book revolved around coal miners during the twentieth century, the underlined sentence does not focus on a major historical event during this time.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1743430669205,"updateDate":1743430669205}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430669205, 1743430669205),
    ($SATQ$7d8224f9$SATQ$, $SATQ$8c664f64-49df-461c-9e0a-e0cdff7d0ad3$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$TSP$SATQ$, $SATQ$Text Structure and Purpose$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>In 1154, Muhammad al-Idrisi completed a collection of maps of the lands known to medieval Arabic and European scholars. This collection was titled <span lang="ar"><em>Al-Kitāb al-Rujārī</em></span> (<em>The Book of Roger</em>), after the Norman king Roger II who hired him to create it. To create the collection, al-Idrisi consulted Arabic and Greek maps and interviewed travelers about the lands they visited. He included these travelers&rsquo; stories alongside the map illustrations.&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"79023fa6-9fb5-4c89-adc5-cff558752b20","content":"<p>To discuss the benefits of studying mapmaking&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"0c7bc540-10be-426b-bef2-6687d33375f4","content":"<p>To explain how travelers created maps&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"a2f9e782-9e94-475c-9336-c88c1ac4e728","content":"<p>To describe a collection of medieval maps and how it was created</p>"},{"id":"8c21749c-223d-4e04-9697-7d9ae6ff9739","content":"<p>To compare medieval Arabic and Greek mapmaking techniques</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["a2f9e782-9e94-475c-9336-c88c1ac4e728"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer because it most accurately states the main purpose of the text, which is to describe a collection of medieval maps and how it was created. The text begins by mentioning Muhammad al-Idrisi&rsquo;s collection of maps of lands known to medieval Arabic and European scholars. It then states that the Norman king Roger II hired al-Idrisi to create the collection and details al-Idrisi&rsquo;s methods of creation: consulting Arabic and Greek maps and interviewing travelers. In short, the text presents a collection of medieval maps and then goes on to describe how that collection came to be.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the text describes a collection of maps and the process of creating that collection but does not discuss the benefits of studying mapmaking in general. Choice B is incorrect because though the text mentions that al-Idrisi interviewed travelers, the text does not describe how those travelers created maps. Choice D is incorrect because though the text mentions that al-Idrisi consulted Arabic and Greek maps, the text does not offer a comparison of Arabic and Greek mapmaking techniques.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"7d8224f9","external_id":"8c664f64-49df-461c-9e0a-e0cdff7d0ad3","vaultid":null,"uId":"1ae2ad8e-208a-49a9-8815-6724ef54cba3","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"TSP","skill_desc":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>In 1154, Muhammad al-Idrisi completed a collection of maps of the lands known to medieval Arabic and European scholars. This collection was titled <span lang=\"ar\"><em>Al-Kitāb al-Rujārī</em></span> (<em>The Book of Roger</em>), after the Norman king Roger II who hired him to create it. To create the collection, al-Idrisi consulted Arabic and Greek maps and interviewed travelers about the lands they visited. He included these travelers&rsquo; stories alongside the map illustrations.&nbsp;</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"79023fa6-9fb5-4c89-adc5-cff558752b20","content":"<p>To discuss the benefits of studying mapmaking&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"0c7bc540-10be-426b-bef2-6687d33375f4","content":"<p>To explain how travelers created maps&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"a2f9e782-9e94-475c-9336-c88c1ac4e728","content":"<p>To describe a collection of medieval maps and how it was created</p>"},{"id":"8c21749c-223d-4e04-9697-7d9ae6ff9739","content":"<p>To compare medieval Arabic and Greek mapmaking techniques</p>"}],"keys":["a2f9e782-9e94-475c-9336-c88c1ac4e728"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer because it most accurately states the main purpose of the text, which is to describe a collection of medieval maps and how it was created. The text begins by mentioning Muhammad al-Idrisi&rsquo;s collection of maps of lands known to medieval Arabic and European scholars. It then states that the Norman king Roger II hired al-Idrisi to create the collection and details al-Idrisi&rsquo;s methods of creation: consulting Arabic and Greek maps and interviewing travelers. In short, the text presents a collection of medieval maps and then goes on to describe how that collection came to be.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the text describes a collection of maps and the process of creating that collection but does not discuss the benefits of studying mapmaking in general. Choice B is incorrect because though the text mentions that al-Idrisi interviewed travelers, the text does not describe how those travelers created maps. Choice D is incorrect because though the text mentions that al-Idrisi consulted Arabic and Greek maps, the text does not offer a comparison of Arabic and Greek mapmaking techniques.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1730147323041,"updateDate":1730147323041}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147323041, 1730147323041),
    ($SATQ$7d84fe2b$SATQ$, $SATQ$73f9ca81-f6b5-49ab-9b9e-7b80671f70cd$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$2d6ae191-3a4e-4c02-85a5-af8ce2eca322$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Particle physicists like Ayana Holloway Arce and Aida El-Khadra spend much of their time <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> what is invisible to the naked eye: using sophisticated technology, they closely examine the behavior of subatomic particles, the smallest detectable parts of matter.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"f27a88fb-e1f4-4fae-82e7-b80df99904ea","content":"<p>selecting</p>"},{"id":"19dd41d4-6221-49de-b26a-d552054f3484","content":"<p>inspecting</p>"},{"id":"2a5ae72b-8dc2-4b93-813e-1410870a15a4","content":"<p>creating</p>"},{"id":"5d20f537-a0ae-4994-97c6-6f54db252080","content":"<p>deciding</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["19dd41d4-6221-49de-b26a-d552054f3484"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the work of particle physicists. In this context, &ldquo;inspecting&rdquo; means viewing closely in order to examine. The text indicates that as particle physicists, Arce and El-Khadra&rsquo;s work involves using advanced technology to &ldquo;closely examine&rdquo; subatomic particles. In other words, they use technology to inspect small parts of matter that can&rsquo;t be seen by the naked eye. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because nothing in the text suggests that Arce and El-Khadra spend time &ldquo;selecting,&rdquo; or choosing, subatomic particles for some purpose; the text simply states that the particle physicists use advanced technology to see and study the behavior of those tiny parts of matter. Choice C is incorrect because nothing in the text suggests that Arce and El-Khadra spend time &ldquo;creating&rdquo; subatomic particles, or bringing them into existence; the text simply states that the particle physicists use advanced technology to see and study the behavior of those tiny parts of matter. Choice D is incorrect. In this context, &ldquo;deciding&rdquo; would mean making a final choice or judgment about something. It wouldn&rsquo;t make sense to say that particle physicists get to choose what is and isn&rsquo;t visible to the naked eye, especially when the text presents it as fact that subatomic particles are &ldquo;the smallest detectable parts of matter&rdquo; and would therefore be invisible. The text focuses on Arce and El-Khadra&rsquo;s close observation of those particles, not on any decisions they might make.&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-956-WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$34b796ca-ca60-4e16-8442-8ae2b166f161$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"7d84fe2b","external_id":"73f9ca81-f6b5-49ab-9b9e-7b80671f70cd","vaultid":"2d6ae191-3a4e-4c02-85a5-af8ce2eca322","uId":"3f890264-8823-468d-86cf-d7d91d92a49a","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Particle physicists like Ayana Holloway Arce and Aida El-Khadra spend much of their time <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> what is invisible to the naked eye: using sophisticated technology, they closely examine the behavior of subatomic particles, the smallest detectable parts of matter.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"f27a88fb-e1f4-4fae-82e7-b80df99904ea","content":"<p>selecting</p>"},{"id":"19dd41d4-6221-49de-b26a-d552054f3484","content":"<p>inspecting</p>"},{"id":"2a5ae72b-8dc2-4b93-813e-1410870a15a4","content":"<p>creating</p>"},{"id":"5d20f537-a0ae-4994-97c6-6f54db252080","content":"<p>deciding</p>"}],"keys":["19dd41d4-6221-49de-b26a-d552054f3484"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the work of particle physicists. In this context, &ldquo;inspecting&rdquo; means viewing closely in order to examine. The text indicates that as particle physicists, Arce and El-Khadra&rsquo;s work involves using advanced technology to &ldquo;closely examine&rdquo; subatomic particles. In other words, they use technology to inspect small parts of matter that can&rsquo;t be seen by the naked eye. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because nothing in the text suggests that Arce and El-Khadra spend time &ldquo;selecting,&rdquo; or choosing, subatomic particles for some purpose; the text simply states that the particle physicists use advanced technology to see and study the behavior of those tiny parts of matter. Choice C is incorrect because nothing in the text suggests that Arce and El-Khadra spend time &ldquo;creating&rdquo; subatomic particles, or bringing them into existence; the text simply states that the particle physicists use advanced technology to see and study the behavior of those tiny parts of matter. Choice D is incorrect. In this context, &ldquo;deciding&rdquo; would mean making a final choice or judgment about something. It wouldn&rsquo;t make sense to say that particle physicists get to choose what is and isn&rsquo;t visible to the naked eye, especially when the text presents it as fact that subatomic particles are &ldquo;the smallest detectable parts of matter&rdquo; and would therefore be invisible. The text focuses on Arce and El-Khadra&rsquo;s close observation of those particles, not on any decisions they might make.&nbsp;</p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-956-WIC","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"34b796ca-ca60-4e16-8442-8ae2b166f161","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959356,"updateDate":1691007959356}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959356, 1691007959356),
    ($SATQ$7f935017$SATQ$, $SATQ$7a84daaf-4322-4bdc-aed9-b52f165cfc97$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The following text is from a 1955 translation of Samuel Beckett&rsquo;s 1951 novel <em>Molloy</em> (translated by the author and Patrick Bowles). In the text, Molloy has arrived at the town ramparts, an elevated walkway atop the city walls.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>And having cleared the ramparts I had to confess the sky was clearing, prior to its winding in the other shroud, night. Yes, the great cloud was ravelling, discovering here and there a pale and dying sky, and the sun, already down, was <span style="text-decoration: underline;" role="region" aria-label="Referenced Content">manifest</span> in the livid tongues of fire darting towards the zenith, falling and darting again, ever more pale and languid, and doomed no sooner lit to be extinguished.</p>
</blockquote>
<p style="text-align: right;"><span class="dap_copyright">&copy;1955 by Grove Press, Inc.</span></p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>As used in the text, what does the word &ldquo;manifest&rdquo; most nearly mean?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"3f32f623-7c0c-4a80-8975-13db6264c545","content":"<p>Realized</p>"},{"id":"2bf519af-ad5f-4f83-b2ca-8bd7b3a9d5c5","content":"<p>Perceptible</p>"},{"id":"b2705fcc-53f2-4e62-be7b-756f375d8f57","content":"<p>Situated</p>"},{"id":"625c73d8-03cd-4d2a-a5ae-18fa39e7e693","content":"<p>Dwindling</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["2bf519af-ad5f-4f83-b2ca-8bd7b3a9d5c5"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer because as used in the text, &ldquo;manifest&rdquo; most nearly means perceptible or detectable. The text indicates that the sun was &ldquo;already down,&rdquo; meaning it was below the horizon and not directly visible. However, the sun&rsquo;s presence was nonetheless perceptible or manifest in the &ldquo;tongues of fire&rdquo; (or beams of light) that still flickered in the darkening sky.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. Although in some contexts &ldquo;manifest&rdquo; can mean &ldquo;realized&rdquo; or &ldquo;brought into being,&rdquo; that is not the context here. Rather, the text is about how the sun&rsquo;s presence was perceptible or manifest in the &ldquo;darting&rdquo; beams of light that could still be seen in the sky. Choice C is incorrect. This choice would suggest that the sun is situated, or located, in the light it emits, which is not supported by the surrounding context. Rather, the text is about how the sun&rsquo;s presence was perceptible or manifest in the remaining light that could still be seen in the sky. Choice D is incorrect. Although the text is about the decreasing light in the scene at sunset, the text&rsquo;s use of &ldquo;manifest&rdquo; is about how the sun&rsquo;s presence was nonetheless perceptible or manifest in the &ldquo;tongues of fire&rdquo; still visible in the sky as night approached.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"7f935017","external_id":"7a84daaf-4322-4bdc-aed9-b52f165cfc97","vaultid":null,"uId":"3d9ee449-2c58-45f9-9e0b-982e88fe1b4d","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>The following text is from a 1955 translation of Samuel Beckett&rsquo;s 1951 novel <em>Molloy</em> (translated by the author and Patrick Bowles). In the text, Molloy has arrived at the town ramparts, an elevated walkway atop the city walls.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>And having cleared the ramparts I had to confess the sky was clearing, prior to its winding in the other shroud, night. Yes, the great cloud was ravelling, discovering here and there a pale and dying sky, and the sun, already down, was <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Referenced Content\">manifest</span> in the livid tongues of fire darting towards the zenith, falling and darting again, ever more pale and languid, and doomed no sooner lit to be extinguished.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p style=\"text-align: right;\"><span class=\"dap_copyright\">&copy;1955 by Grove Press, Inc.</span></p>","stem":"<p>As used in the text, what does the word &ldquo;manifest&rdquo; most nearly mean?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"3f32f623-7c0c-4a80-8975-13db6264c545","content":"<p>Realized</p>"},{"id":"2bf519af-ad5f-4f83-b2ca-8bd7b3a9d5c5","content":"<p>Perceptible</p>"},{"id":"b2705fcc-53f2-4e62-be7b-756f375d8f57","content":"<p>Situated</p>"},{"id":"625c73d8-03cd-4d2a-a5ae-18fa39e7e693","content":"<p>Dwindling</p>"}],"keys":["2bf519af-ad5f-4f83-b2ca-8bd7b3a9d5c5"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer because as used in the text, &ldquo;manifest&rdquo; most nearly means perceptible or detectable. The text indicates that the sun was &ldquo;already down,&rdquo; meaning it was below the horizon and not directly visible. However, the sun&rsquo;s presence was nonetheless perceptible or manifest in the &ldquo;tongues of fire&rdquo; (or beams of light) that still flickered in the darkening sky.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. Although in some contexts &ldquo;manifest&rdquo; can mean &ldquo;realized&rdquo; or &ldquo;brought into being,&rdquo; that is not the context here. Rather, the text is about how the sun&rsquo;s presence was perceptible or manifest in the &ldquo;darting&rdquo; beams of light that could still be seen in the sky. Choice C is incorrect. This choice would suggest that the sun is situated, or located, in the light it emits, which is not supported by the surrounding context. Rather, the text is about how the sun&rsquo;s presence was perceptible or manifest in the remaining light that could still be seen in the sky. Choice D is incorrect. Although the text is about the decreasing light in the scene at sunset, the text&rsquo;s use of &ldquo;manifest&rdquo; is about how the sun&rsquo;s presence was nonetheless perceptible or manifest in the &ldquo;tongues of fire&rdquo; still visible in the sky as night approached.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1776362771169,"updateDate":1776362771169}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1776362771169, 1776362771169),
    ($SATQ$805e361d$SATQ$, $SATQ$f01d6e44-be79-4f67-896e-a96a00d7112b$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$TSP$SATQ$, $SATQ$Text Structure and Purpose$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Companies are providing consumers with more opportunities to purchase customized products than ever before. Whether buying customized sneakers, jewelry, or clothing, consumers can participate in the design of products to meet their specific needs and tastes. In turn, companies profit too: studies have shown that consumers are willing to pay more and wait longer for a customized product. Still, it can be difficult for companies to offer customization while keeping costs low, as the standard methods of mass production may not be able to accommodate making a unique product each time.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"2dfb0aff-b2db-4ce2-b214-bbb293f6932c","content":"<p>It discusses several recent innovations in product manufacturing and then suggests some potential applications of those innovations.</p>"},{"id":"47281f9f-afdc-4801-99af-444ef1cbc12b","content":"<p>It describes a company&rsquo;s recent success with new products and then explains multiple factors that may have contributed to that success.</p>"},{"id":"a20d17a4-3035-496d-951a-6f33ce44e139","content":"<p>It introduces a trend in consumer products and then explains how the trend both benefits and poses a challenge to companies.</p>"},{"id":"02cfddcc-3b3f-4212-8574-e50151736b41","content":"<p>It presents two contrasting product-marketing techniques and then provides examples of one of those techniques.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["a20d17a4-3035-496d-951a-6f33ce44e139"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer because it presents the best description of the overall structure of the text. The text begins by stating that companies are increasingly giving consumers opportunities to customize products, allowing them to make design choices when buying certain sneakers, jewelry, and clothing. The text then indicates that although this trend benefits companies because they can successfully charge buyers more for customized products and don&rsquo;t have to rush production, it also poses a challenge because producing unique items may require different and more expensive methods than the ones typically used for mass production, raising the companies&rsquo; costs. Thus, the text first introduces a trend in consumer products and then explains how the trend both benefits and poses a challenge to companies.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the text doesn&rsquo;t present the customization of various products as a recent innovation&mdash;the fact that there are "more opportunities" now indicates that there were opportunities before&mdash;and no other innovations, in product manufacturing or otherwise, are discussed. Choice B is incorrect because the text doesn&rsquo;t discuss any particular company or example and instead speaks broadly about the trend of companies providing customizable products. Choice D is incorrect. Although the text discusses companies offering something that consumers like and are willing to pay more for&mdash;the ability to customize products&mdash;it doesn&rsquo;t characterize this as a product-marketing technique and doesn&rsquo;t compare it to any other kind of offering or technique.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"805e361d","external_id":"f01d6e44-be79-4f67-896e-a96a00d7112b","vaultid":null,"uId":"2a2016ca-71fa-44f3-a3d6-b35f3b0bcf9f","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"TSP","skill_desc":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>Companies are providing consumers with more opportunities to purchase customized products than ever before. Whether buying customized sneakers, jewelry, or clothing, consumers can participate in the design of products to meet their specific needs and tastes. In turn, companies profit too: studies have shown that consumers are willing to pay more and wait longer for a customized product. Still, it can be difficult for companies to offer customization while keeping costs low, as the standard methods of mass production may not be able to accommodate making a unique product each time.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"2dfb0aff-b2db-4ce2-b214-bbb293f6932c","content":"<p>It discusses several recent innovations in product manufacturing and then suggests some potential applications of those innovations.</p>"},{"id":"47281f9f-afdc-4801-99af-444ef1cbc12b","content":"<p>It describes a company&rsquo;s recent success with new products and then explains multiple factors that may have contributed to that success.</p>"},{"id":"a20d17a4-3035-496d-951a-6f33ce44e139","content":"<p>It introduces a trend in consumer products and then explains how the trend both benefits and poses a challenge to companies.</p>"},{"id":"02cfddcc-3b3f-4212-8574-e50151736b41","content":"<p>It presents two contrasting product-marketing techniques and then provides examples of one of those techniques.</p>"}],"keys":["a20d17a4-3035-496d-951a-6f33ce44e139"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer because it presents the best description of the overall structure of the text. The text begins by stating that companies are increasingly giving consumers opportunities to customize products, allowing them to make design choices when buying certain sneakers, jewelry, and clothing. The text then indicates that although this trend benefits companies because they can successfully charge buyers more for customized products and don&rsquo;t have to rush production, it also poses a challenge because producing unique items may require different and more expensive methods than the ones typically used for mass production, raising the companies&rsquo; costs. Thus, the text first introduces a trend in consumer products and then explains how the trend both benefits and poses a challenge to companies.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the text doesn&rsquo;t present the customization of various products as a recent innovation&mdash;the fact that there are \"more opportunities\" now indicates that there were opportunities before&mdash;and no other innovations, in product manufacturing or otherwise, are discussed. Choice B is incorrect because the text doesn&rsquo;t discuss any particular company or example and instead speaks broadly about the trend of companies providing customizable products. Choice D is incorrect. Although the text discusses companies offering something that consumers like and are willing to pay more for&mdash;the ability to customize products&mdash;it doesn&rsquo;t characterize this as a product-marketing technique and doesn&rsquo;t compare it to any other kind of offering or technique.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1743430669215,"updateDate":1743430669215}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430669215, 1743430669215),
    ($SATQ$809addda$SATQ$, $SATQ$c0d5cda2-7f7f-4ff4-8770-c67f7547c647$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$TSP$SATQ$, $SATQ$Text Structure and Purpose$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The following text is from Ameen Rihani&rsquo;s 1921 poem &ldquo;The Wanderer.&rdquo;&nbsp;</p>
<blockquote class="dap_poemexcerpt">
<p>I wander among the hills of alien lands</p>
<p style="padding-left: 1em;">Where Nature her prerogative resigns</p>
<p>To Man; where Comfort in her shack reclines</p>
<p style="padding-left: 1em;">And all the arts and sciences commands.</p>
<div role="region" aria-label="Referenced Content">
<p style="padding-left: 2em;"><span style="text-decoration: underline;">But in my soul</span></p>
<p style="padding-left: 2em;"><span style="text-decoration: underline;">The eastern billows roll&mdash;</span></p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">I hear the voices of my native strands.</span></p>
</div>
</blockquote>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice best describes the function of the underlined lines in the text as a whole?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"b5c8a24f-5572-4075-8bce-9f0f42b3ad10","content":"<p>It establishes that the speaker&rsquo;s enthusiasm about current travels conflicts with the growing urge to return home.</p>"},{"id":"727aa152-125d-4a60-8ce2-0aa5a9716140","content":"<p>It illustrates the speaker&rsquo;s uncertainty about maintaining strong links with relatives in distant places.</p>"},{"id":"4bd1afe2-88c3-404f-b3b3-3dd0f1dfaa7b","content":"<p>It conveys the speaker&rsquo;s sense of feeling a pull toward home while traveling in an unfamiliar place.</p>"},{"id":"bcd5c735-98c9-49af-a4cb-41cb5c7b4eef","content":"<p>It reveals that upon returning after an extended absence, the speaker longs for the way a location once felt.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["4bd1afe2-88c3-404f-b3b3-3dd0f1dfaa7b"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer because it most accurately describes the function of the underlined lines in the text as a whole. In the opening line of the text, the speaker describes wandering in "alien lands," which establishes that the speaker is traveling in unfamiliar territory. In the underlined lines, the speaker describes "billows" (large waves) rolling in the soul, which suggests that the speaker feels inner turmoil. The underlined lines go on to associate these rolling billows with voices calling to the speaker from the speaker&rsquo;s "native strands," or homeland, indicating that thoughts of home are prompting the emotional experience these lines describe. Taken together, the imagery in the underlined lines thus implies that the speaker feels a deep emotional connection to, or pull toward, home while traveling in an unfamiliar place.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. While the text&rsquo;s first line states that the speaker is traveling and the underlined lines indicate that the speaker experiences an emotional pull toward home, neither the underlined lines nor the text as a whole establishes an enthusiasm about the current travels that conflicts with a growing urge to return home. The text&rsquo;s description of the lands the speaker is traveling in focuses on their artificial quality, stating, "Nature her prerogative resigns / To Man," which doesn&rsquo;t suggest enthusiasm but rather a sense of detachment or even critique. Choice B is incorrect because the underlined lines don&rsquo;t address uncertainty about maintaining links with relatives in distant places. In the underlined lines, the speaker expresses a sense of connection to the speaker&rsquo;s homeland ("native strands") but doesn&rsquo;t refer to any family members the speaker may have there or to concerns about maintaining any familial ties. Choice D is incorrect because the poem doesn&rsquo;t indicate that the speaker has returned home after an absence. Rather, the speaker explicitly states, "I wander among the hills of alien lands," establishing that the current setting is a foreign place. Moreover, the underlined lines express a sense of connection with, or pull toward, a distant homeland, not a sense of longing for how that homeland or any other location once felt.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"809addda","external_id":"c0d5cda2-7f7f-4ff4-8770-c67f7547c647","vaultid":null,"uId":"625c02d2-0bcb-44a8-a217-9c702d07ff3e","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"TSP","skill_desc":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>The following text is from Ameen Rihani&rsquo;s 1921 poem &ldquo;The Wanderer.&rdquo;&nbsp;</p>\n<blockquote class=\"dap_poemexcerpt\">\n<p>I wander among the hills of alien lands</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 1em;\">Where Nature her prerogative resigns</p>\n<p>To Man; where Comfort in her shack reclines</p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 1em;\">And all the arts and sciences commands.</p>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Referenced Content\">\n<p style=\"padding-left: 2em;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">But in my soul</span></p>\n<p style=\"padding-left: 2em;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">The eastern billows roll&mdash;</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">I hear the voices of my native strands.</span></p>\n</div>\n</blockquote>","stem":"<p>Which choice best describes the function of the underlined lines in the text as a whole?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"b5c8a24f-5572-4075-8bce-9f0f42b3ad10","content":"<p>It establishes that the speaker&rsquo;s enthusiasm about current travels conflicts with the growing urge to return home.</p>"},{"id":"727aa152-125d-4a60-8ce2-0aa5a9716140","content":"<p>It illustrates the speaker&rsquo;s uncertainty about maintaining strong links with relatives in distant places.</p>"},{"id":"4bd1afe2-88c3-404f-b3b3-3dd0f1dfaa7b","content":"<p>It conveys the speaker&rsquo;s sense of feeling a pull toward home while traveling in an unfamiliar place.</p>"},{"id":"bcd5c735-98c9-49af-a4cb-41cb5c7b4eef","content":"<p>It reveals that upon returning after an extended absence, the speaker longs for the way a location once felt.</p>"}],"keys":["4bd1afe2-88c3-404f-b3b3-3dd0f1dfaa7b"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer because it most accurately describes the function of the underlined lines in the text as a whole. In the opening line of the text, the speaker describes wandering in \"alien lands,\" which establishes that the speaker is traveling in unfamiliar territory. In the underlined lines, the speaker describes \"billows\" (large waves) rolling in the soul, which suggests that the speaker feels inner turmoil. The underlined lines go on to associate these rolling billows with voices calling to the speaker from the speaker&rsquo;s \"native strands,\" or homeland, indicating that thoughts of home are prompting the emotional experience these lines describe. Taken together, the imagery in the underlined lines thus implies that the speaker feels a deep emotional connection to, or pull toward, home while traveling in an unfamiliar place.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. While the text&rsquo;s first line states that the speaker is traveling and the underlined lines indicate that the speaker experiences an emotional pull toward home, neither the underlined lines nor the text as a whole establishes an enthusiasm about the current travels that conflicts with a growing urge to return home. The text&rsquo;s description of the lands the speaker is traveling in focuses on their artificial quality, stating, \"Nature her prerogative resigns / To Man,\" which doesn&rsquo;t suggest enthusiasm but rather a sense of detachment or even critique. Choice B is incorrect because the underlined lines don&rsquo;t address uncertainty about maintaining links with relatives in distant places. In the underlined lines, the speaker expresses a sense of connection to the speaker&rsquo;s homeland (\"native strands\") but doesn&rsquo;t refer to any family members the speaker may have there or to concerns about maintaining any familial ties. Choice D is incorrect because the poem doesn&rsquo;t indicate that the speaker has returned home after an absence. Rather, the speaker explicitly states, \"I wander among the hills of alien lands,\" establishing that the current setting is a foreign place. Moreover, the underlined lines express a sense of connection with, or pull toward, a distant homeland, not a sense of longing for how that homeland or any other location once felt.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"createDate":1755117061191,"updateDate":1755117061191}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117061191, 1755117061191),
    ($SATQ$80ebb189$SATQ$, $SATQ$4afe3db2-b623-42c2-85aa-cab808b4b049$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$3e7df5bd-934f-4880-b427-39b276d3fa5b$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>As an architect in Los Angeles in the 1950s, Helen Liu Fong became known for avoiding <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> designs in her buildings. Instead of using standard shapes and colors, she typically explored innovative forms and daring hues.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"8d54ae8f-f761-4e81-aa69-1deed3969dee","content":"<p>creative</p>"},{"id":"4f8f2bd8-fe66-4944-9791-a5f1bbb71c06","content":"<p>bold</p>"},{"id":"9f5b7817-fdeb-4e5e-a966-749b92deb4e1","content":"<p>traditional</p>"},{"id":"3af8341c-647e-4294-bb08-70c60830e40a","content":"<p>understandable</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["9f5b7817-fdeb-4e5e-a966-749b92deb4e1"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of Helen Liu Fong&rsquo;s architectural designs. In this context, &ldquo;traditional&rdquo; means conventional. The text states that rather than use &ldquo;standard shapes and colors,&rdquo; Fong pursued &ldquo;innovative&rdquo; and &ldquo;daring&rdquo; design choices in her work. Fong&rsquo;s style is depicted as inventive, so it therefore makes sense in this context that she avoided mainstream, traditional designs in her buildings.&nbsp;</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the text indicates that Fong&rsquo;s work is innovative and experimental. Thus, Fong&rsquo;s design choices could reasonably be considered creative, or original. She likely would have pursued creative designs, not avoided them. Choice B is incorrect because the text indicates that Fong used &ldquo;daring&rdquo; hues in her designs. Thus, Fong likely would have pursued bold, or brave and vivid design choices; she wouldn&rsquo;t have avoided them. Choice D is incorrect because the text doesn&rsquo;t address whether Fong&rsquo;s designs are understandable, or reasonable or expected. The text focuses on certain characteristics of Fong&rsquo;s designs, not on how people received or understood them. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-024-WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$de9651ac-7e95-407c-93c6-8256fc450885$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"80ebb189","external_id":"4afe3db2-b623-42c2-85aa-cab808b4b049","vaultid":"3e7df5bd-934f-4880-b427-39b276d3fa5b","uId":"93552757-8802-4f61-8921-121f05210826","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>As an architect in Los Angeles in the 1950s, Helen Liu Fong became known for avoiding <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> designs in her buildings. Instead of using standard shapes and colors, she typically explored innovative forms and daring hues.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"8d54ae8f-f761-4e81-aa69-1deed3969dee","content":"<p>creative</p>"},{"id":"4f8f2bd8-fe66-4944-9791-a5f1bbb71c06","content":"<p>bold</p>"},{"id":"9f5b7817-fdeb-4e5e-a966-749b92deb4e1","content":"<p>traditional</p>"},{"id":"3af8341c-647e-4294-bb08-70c60830e40a","content":"<p>understandable</p>"}],"keys":["9f5b7817-fdeb-4e5e-a966-749b92deb4e1"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of Helen Liu Fong&rsquo;s architectural designs. In this context, &ldquo;traditional&rdquo; means conventional. The text states that rather than use &ldquo;standard shapes and colors,&rdquo; Fong pursued &ldquo;innovative&rdquo; and &ldquo;daring&rdquo; design choices in her work. Fong&rsquo;s style is depicted as inventive, so it therefore makes sense in this context that she avoided mainstream, traditional designs in her buildings.&nbsp;</p><p>Choice A is incorrect because the text indicates that Fong&rsquo;s work is innovative and experimental. Thus, Fong&rsquo;s design choices could reasonably be considered creative, or original. She likely would have pursued creative designs, not avoided them. Choice B is incorrect because the text indicates that Fong used &ldquo;daring&rdquo; hues in her designs. Thus, Fong likely would have pursued bold, or brave and vivid design choices; she wouldn&rsquo;t have avoided them. Choice D is incorrect because the text doesn&rsquo;t address whether Fong&rsquo;s designs are understandable, or reasonable or expected. The text focuses on certain characteristics of Fong&rsquo;s designs, not on how people received or understood them. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-024-WIC","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"de9651ac-7e95-407c-93c6-8256fc450885","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959318,"updateDate":1691007959318}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959318, 1691007959318),
    ($SATQ$81a3a607$SATQ$, $SATQ$c5e5c8c2-3f39-450b-907e-e7983208d347$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$3085ae6e-a238-44b8-8a61-bfa84139b925$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>In the Indigenous intercropping system known as the Three Sisters, maize, squash, and beans form an <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> web of relations: maize provides the structure on which the bean vines grow; the squash vines cover the soil, discouraging competition from weeds; and the beans aid their two &ldquo;sisters&rdquo; by enriching the soil with essential nitrogen.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"24b6e276-f6f8-4b9b-848a-ca3c02d831c4","content":"<p>indecipherable</p>"},{"id":"3698d0f4-b425-454c-8aae-2f412e54b37f","content":"<p>ornamental</p>"},{"id":"e3ae1073-f022-4bc8-81ac-0dc23ef4ab31","content":"<p>obscure</p>"},{"id":"07f62782-68ac-43bb-bea9-23b7f7a47a8e","content":"<p>intricate</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["07f62782-68ac-43bb-bea9-23b7f7a47a8e"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the Three Sisters intercropping system. As used in this context, &ldquo;intricate&rdquo; would mean made up of complexly related elements. The text indicates that in the Three Sisters system, maize, squash, and beans form a &ldquo;web of relations&rdquo; in which the crops interact in various ways. The text&rsquo;s description of these interactions&mdash;the bean vines growing on the maize stalks, the squash vines keeping weeds away, and the beans adding nutrients that the maize and squash use&mdash;provides context suggesting that this &ldquo;web of relations&rdquo; is intricate. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because describing the relationship among the crops in the Three Sisters system as &ldquo;indecipherable,&rdquo; or impossible to comprehend, would not make sense in context. Although the text presents the relationship as complex, the text&rsquo;s description of the role that each crop plays makes it clear that the relationship is well understood, not indecipherable.&nbsp;Choice B is incorrect because the text discusses the practical benefits that each plant in the Three Sisters system provides to other members of the system, showing that the relationship among the crops that make up the system is not &ldquo;ornamental,&rdquo; or mainly serving a decorative purpose. Choice C is incorrect because describing the relationship among the crops in the Three Sisters system as &ldquo;obscure,&rdquo; or unknown or poorly understood, would not make sense in context. Although the text presents the relationship as complex, the text&rsquo;s description of the role that each crop plays makes it clear that the relationship is well understood, not obscure.&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-939-WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$6adf7a7f-ecc3-4611-b85c-62e6a521dd23$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"81a3a607","external_id":"c5e5c8c2-3f39-450b-907e-e7983208d347","vaultid":"3085ae6e-a238-44b8-8a61-bfa84139b925","uId":"82580ebf-eb7e-4dc4-8068-7ffee6495b89","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>In the Indigenous intercropping system known as the Three Sisters, maize, squash, and beans form an <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> web of relations: maize provides the structure on which the bean vines grow; the squash vines cover the soil, discouraging competition from weeds; and the beans aid their two &ldquo;sisters&rdquo; by enriching the soil with essential nitrogen.</p>","stem":"<p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"24b6e276-f6f8-4b9b-848a-ca3c02d831c4","content":"<p>indecipherable</p>"},{"id":"3698d0f4-b425-454c-8aae-2f412e54b37f","content":"<p>ornamental</p>"},{"id":"e3ae1073-f022-4bc8-81ac-0dc23ef4ab31","content":"<p>obscure</p>"},{"id":"07f62782-68ac-43bb-bea9-23b7f7a47a8e","content":"<p>intricate</p>"}],"keys":["07f62782-68ac-43bb-bea9-23b7f7a47a8e"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer because it most logically completes the text&rsquo;s discussion of the Three Sisters intercropping system. As used in this context, &ldquo;intricate&rdquo; would mean made up of complexly related elements. The text indicates that in the Three Sisters system, maize, squash, and beans form a &ldquo;web of relations&rdquo; in which the crops interact in various ways. The text&rsquo;s description of these interactions&mdash;the bean vines growing on the maize stalks, the squash vines keeping weeds away, and the beans adding nutrients that the maize and squash use&mdash;provides context suggesting that this &ldquo;web of relations&rdquo; is intricate. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect because describing the relationship among the crops in the Three Sisters system as &ldquo;indecipherable,&rdquo; or impossible to comprehend, would not make sense in context. Although the text presents the relationship as complex, the text&rsquo;s description of the role that each crop plays makes it clear that the relationship is well understood, not indecipherable.&nbsp;Choice B is incorrect because the text discusses the practical benefits that each plant in the Three Sisters system provides to other members of the system, showing that the relationship among the crops that make up the system is not &ldquo;ornamental,&rdquo; or mainly serving a decorative purpose. Choice C is incorrect because describing the relationship among the crops in the Three Sisters system as &ldquo;obscure,&rdquo; or unknown or poorly understood, would not make sense in context. Although the text presents the relationship as complex, the text&rsquo;s description of the role that each crop plays makes it clear that the relationship is well understood, not obscure.&nbsp;</p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-939-WIC","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"6adf7a7f-ecc3-4611-b85c-62e6a521dd23","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959356,"updateDate":1691007959356}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959356, 1691007959356),
    ($SATQ$81da17d3$SATQ$, $SATQ$62c97dfc-439e-441e-8088-c793d4e73986$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$4f353359-f913-4544-9062-ff169b1c5e61$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$CTC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Cross-Text Connections$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p><strong>Text 1</strong></p>
<p>Italian painters in the 1500s rarely depicted themselves in their work. Even more rare were self-portrait paintings that portrayed the artist as a painter. At the time, painting was not yet respected as a profession, so painters mostly chose to emphasize other qualities in their self-portraits, like their intellect or social status. <span style="text-decoration: underline;">In the city of Bologna, the first artist to depict themself painting was a man named Annibale Carracci.</span> A painting of his from around 1585 shows Carracci in front of an easel holding a palette.&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Text 2</strong></p>
<p>In their self-portraits, Bolognese artists typically avoided referring to the act of painting until the mid-1600s. However, Lavinia Fontana&rsquo;s 1577 painting, <em>Self-Portrait at the Keyboard</em>, stands out as the earliest example of such a work by an artist from Bologna. Although the artist is depicted playing music, in the background, one can spot a painting easel by a window.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the underlined claim in Text 1?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"771c1da6-fff5-4db0-84bc-d959a4b60684","content":"<p>Carracci and Fontana were among the most well-respected painters in Bologna at the time.</p>"},{"id":"441a721e-f6dc-4bc6-8aad-532e2dba1b8f","content":"<p>The depiction of Fontana in <em>Self-Portrait at the Keyboard</em> was intended to underscore the artist&rsquo;s creativity.</p>"},{"id":"9be1c837-a109-4c88-aade-d122e57d8975","content":"<p>Fontana likely inspired the reference to an easel and palette in Carracci&rsquo;s painting.</p>"},{"id":"3da49cda-ae83-4c2e-b896-2e08f754bae3","content":"<p><em>Self-Portrait at the Keyboard</em> was painted earlier than Carracci&rsquo;s painting and also refers to the artist&rsquo;s craft.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["3da49cda-ae83-4c2e-b896-2e08f754bae3"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is the best answer. The author of Text 2 states that Fontana&rsquo;s painting, which depicts a painting easel in the background, was made in 1577, eight years before Carracci&rsquo;s painting. Therefore, they might argue that Caracci was not &ldquo;the first artist&rdquo; to depict themself as a painter. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The texts don&rsquo;t support this choice. Neither text mentions the reputation or status of either Carracci or Fontana. Choice B is incorrect. The author of Text 2 does not comment on the intention or meaning of Fontana&rsquo;s self-depiction in <em>Self-Portrait at the Keyboard</em>. This choice also holds little connection to the underlined claim. Choice C is incorrect. The texts don&rsquo;t support this choice. The author of Text 2 does not suggest any inspirational relationship between Fontana and Carracci. The author of Text 2 is concerned with showing that Fontana&rsquo;s painting is the earliest example of an artist referring to painting in their self-portrait, but makes no mention of her influence on others. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-CTC-E005$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$a39fda88-9c5d-46a6-a2df-d4b60ac4b2b0$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"81da17d3","external_id":"62c97dfc-439e-441e-8088-c793d4e73986","vaultid":"4f353359-f913-4544-9062-ff169b1c5e61","uId":"2a49d2d5-b6c6-4b88-9182-0c9b19bff079","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"CTC","skill_desc":"Cross-Text Connections","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p><strong>Text 1</strong></p>\n<p>Italian painters in the 1500s rarely depicted themselves in their work. Even more rare were self-portrait paintings that portrayed the artist as a painter. At the time, painting was not yet respected as a profession, so painters mostly chose to emphasize other qualities in their self-portraits, like their intellect or social status. <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">In the city of Bologna, the first artist to depict themself painting was a man named Annibale Carracci.</span> A painting of his from around 1585 shows Carracci in front of an easel holding a palette.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Text 2</strong></p>\n<p>In their self-portraits, Bolognese artists typically avoided referring to the act of painting until the mid-1600s. However, Lavinia Fontana&rsquo;s 1577 painting, <em>Self-Portrait at the Keyboard</em>, stands out as the earliest example of such a work by an artist from Bologna. Although the artist is depicted playing music, in the background, one can spot a painting easel by a window.</p>","stem":"<p>Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the underlined claim in Text 1?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"771c1da6-fff5-4db0-84bc-d959a4b60684","content":"<p>Carracci and Fontana were among the most well-respected painters in Bologna at the time.</p>"},{"id":"441a721e-f6dc-4bc6-8aad-532e2dba1b8f","content":"<p>The depiction of Fontana in <em>Self-Portrait at the Keyboard</em> was intended to underscore the artist&rsquo;s creativity.</p>"},{"id":"9be1c837-a109-4c88-aade-d122e57d8975","content":"<p>Fontana likely inspired the reference to an easel and palette in Carracci&rsquo;s painting.</p>"},{"id":"3da49cda-ae83-4c2e-b896-2e08f754bae3","content":"<p><em>Self-Portrait at the Keyboard</em> was painted earlier than Carracci&rsquo;s painting and also refers to the artist&rsquo;s craft.</p>"}],"keys":["3da49cda-ae83-4c2e-b896-2e08f754bae3"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is the best answer. The author of Text 2 states that Fontana&rsquo;s painting, which depicts a painting easel in the background, was made in 1577, eight years before Carracci&rsquo;s painting. Therefore, they might argue that Caracci was not &ldquo;the first artist&rdquo; to depict themself as a painter. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. The texts don&rsquo;t support this choice. Neither text mentions the reputation or status of either Carracci or Fontana. Choice B is incorrect. The author of Text 2 does not comment on the intention or meaning of Fontana&rsquo;s self-depiction in <em>Self-Portrait at the Keyboard</em>. This choice also holds little connection to the underlined claim. Choice C is incorrect. The texts don&rsquo;t support this choice. The author of Text 2 does not suggest any inspirational relationship between Fontana and Carracci. The author of Text 2 is concerned with showing that Fontana&rsquo;s painting is the earliest example of an artist referring to painting in their self-portrait, but makes no mention of her influence on others. </p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-CTC-E005","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"a39fda88-9c5d-46a6-a2df-d4b60ac4b2b0","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959361,"updateDate":1691007959361}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959361, 1691007959361),
    ($SATQ$82b7c3b2$SATQ$, $SATQ$de5605c6-c05a-4384-b569-7efefdfccbd2$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$1937b3a4-cd1e-4837-b10e-188f6c4003c8$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$WIC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Words in Context$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>The following text is from Booth Tarkington&rsquo;s 1921 novel <em>Alice Adams</em>.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Mrs. Adams had always been fond of vases, she said, and every year her husband&rsquo;s Christmas present to her was a vase of one sort or another&mdash;whatever the clerk showed him, <span role="region" aria-label="Referenced Content"><u>marked</u></span> at about twelve or fourteen dollars.</p>
</blockquote>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>As used in the text, what does the word &ldquo;marked&rdquo; most nearly mean?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"471b2b5c-d583-42a8-856f-73b7b49b77ba","content":"<p>Staged</p>"},{"id":"85c8586d-95db-4c20-b9e5-4b1c3be8b28e","content":"<p>Priced</p>"},{"id":"03efaa06-8019-492c-aaa4-f7b89362c23f","content":"<p>Stained</p>"},{"id":"f2d07622-2ad7-48cb-9351-9ec6a7052d6b","content":"<p>Watched</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["85c8586d-95db-4c20-b9e5-4b1c3be8b28e"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is the best answer. The text suggests that Mrs. Adam&rsquo;s typical Christmas present from her husband was a vase that cost, or was "priced at," about twelve or fourteen dollars.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. This isn&rsquo;t the meaning of "marked" as used here. It wouldn&rsquo;t make sense to say that a vase was "staged at twelve or fourteen dollars." Choice C is incorrect. This isn&rsquo;t the meaning of "marked" as used here. It wouldn&rsquo;t make sense to say that a vase was "stained at twelve or fourteen dollars." Choice D is incorrect. This isn&rsquo;t the meaning of "marked" as used here. It wouldn&rsquo;t make sense to say that a vase was "watched at twelve or fourteen dollars."</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-WIC-E001$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$b5084f8f-7744-4337-9199-93451804a761$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"82b7c3b2","external_id":"de5605c6-c05a-4384-b569-7efefdfccbd2","vaultid":"1937b3a4-cd1e-4837-b10e-188f6c4003c8","uId":"d34656ff-c282-4f30-af0b-029471fd8002","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"WIC","skill_desc":"Words in Context","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p>The following text is from Booth Tarkington&rsquo;s 1921 novel <em>Alice Adams</em>.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Mrs. Adams had always been fond of vases, she said, and every year her husband&rsquo;s Christmas present to her was a vase of one sort or another&mdash;whatever the clerk showed him, <span role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Referenced Content\"><u>marked</u></span> at about twelve or fourteen dollars.</p>\n</blockquote>","stem":"<p>As used in the text, what does the word &ldquo;marked&rdquo; most nearly mean?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"471b2b5c-d583-42a8-856f-73b7b49b77ba","content":"<p>Staged</p>"},{"id":"85c8586d-95db-4c20-b9e5-4b1c3be8b28e","content":"<p>Priced</p>"},{"id":"03efaa06-8019-492c-aaa4-f7b89362c23f","content":"<p>Stained</p>"},{"id":"f2d07622-2ad7-48cb-9351-9ec6a7052d6b","content":"<p>Watched</p>"}],"keys":["85c8586d-95db-4c20-b9e5-4b1c3be8b28e"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is the best answer. The text suggests that Mrs. Adam&rsquo;s typical Christmas present from her husband was a vase that cost, or was \"priced at,\" about twelve or fourteen dollars.</p><p>Choice A is incorrect. This isn&rsquo;t the meaning of \"marked\" as used here. It wouldn&rsquo;t make sense to say that a vase was \"staged at twelve or fourteen dollars.\" Choice C is incorrect. This isn&rsquo;t the meaning of \"marked\" as used here. It wouldn&rsquo;t make sense to say that a vase was \"stained at twelve or fourteen dollars.\" Choice D is incorrect. This isn&rsquo;t the meaning of \"marked\" as used here. It wouldn&rsquo;t make sense to say that a vase was \"watched at twelve or fourteen dollars.\"</p>","parenttemplatename":"OSP-KA-WIC-E001","parenttemplateid":"","templateclusterid":"b5084f8f-7744-4337-9199-93451804a761","templateclustername":"","origin":"proteus","position":"0","createDate":1691007959377,"updateDate":1691007959377}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959377, 1691007959377),
    ($SATQ$82c05b34$SATQ$, $SATQ$f9291899-64c6-42eb-a379-30bc15199332$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$1ec4fdd6-6ba5-4f19-9c2f-8e7139c3b554$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Craft and Structure$SATQ$, $SATQ$CAS$SATQ$, $SATQ$CTC$SATQ$, $SATQ$Cross-Text Connections$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p><strong>Text 1</strong></p>
<p>The live music festival business is growing in event size and genre variety. With so many consumer options, organizers are finding ways to cement festival attendance as a special experience worth sharing. This phenomenon is linked to the growing &ldquo;experiential economy,&rdquo; where many find it gratifying to purchase lived experiences. To ensure a profitable event, venues need to consider the overall consumer experience, not just the band lineup.</p>
<p><strong>Text 2</strong></p>
<p>Music festival appearances are becoming a more important part of musicians&rsquo; careers. One factor in this shift is the rising use of streaming services that allow access to huge numbers of songs for a monthly fee, subsequently reducing sales of full-length albums. With this shift in consumer behavior, musicians are increasingly dependent on revenue from live performances.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Based on the texts, both authors would most likely agree with which statement?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"886c4ccc-e592-4439-85aa-3a66dd54b114","content":"<p>Consumers are more interested in paying subscription fees to stream music than in attending music festivals in person.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"5281ca3a-d5d2-4a97-9f53-9409b4b563a8","content":"<p>Consumers&rsquo; growing interest in purchasing experiences is mostly confined to the music industry.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"0ac4657c-1962-4b2d-bfcd-d48fa72f2c5c","content":"<p>Changing consumer behaviors are leading to changes in music-related businesses.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"c385be7d-6a68-4af3-a2d9-a5578301fe83","content":"<p>The rising consumer demand for live music festivals also generates higher demand for music streaming platforms.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["0ac4657c-1962-4b2d-bfcd-d48fa72f2c5c"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is the best answer. Both authors mention how consumer behaviors have shifted, and how this affects different aspects of the music industry. Text 1 states that consumers enjoy purchasing &ldquo;lived experiences,&rdquo; and that this influences how organizers design music festivals. Text 2 states that consumers are using streaming services more, and that this reduces album sales and increases the importance of live performances for musicians. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. Neither text claims that consumers prefer streaming to festivals, or that these are mutually exclusive options. Text 1 implies that festivals are popular and profitable, and Text 2 never suggests that streaming services diminish the demand for live music. Choice B is incorrect. This choice misreads Text 1, which identifies music festivals as just one example of a broader trend of purchasing &ldquo;lived experiences.&rdquo; Text 2 doesn&rsquo;t mention growing interest in purchasing experiences, in the music industry or otherwise. Choice D is incorrect. Neither text establishes a cause/effect relationship between the demand for festivals and the demand for streaming platforms. Text 1 does not mention streaming platforms at all, and Text 2 does not imply that streaming platforms benefit from the popularity of festivals. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, $SATQ$OSP-KA-CTC-M007$SATQ$, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$7ba9927e-fc30-4da7-a69b-b58299c66d11$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$$SATQ$, $SATQ$proteus$SATQ$, $SATQ$0$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"82c05b34","external_id":"f9291899-64c6-42eb-a379-30bc15199332","vaultid":"1ec4fdd6-6ba5-4f19-9c2f-8e7139c3b554","uId":"630289be-5714-4f3f-9123-e84ca4d2586f","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"CAS","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill_cd":"CTC","skill_desc":"Cross-Text Connections","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<p><strong>Text 1</strong></p>\n<p>The live music festival business is growing in event size and genre variety. With so many consumer options, organizers are finding ways to cement festival attendance as a special experience worth sharing. This phenomenon is linked to the growing &ldquo;experiential economy,&rdquo; where many find it gratifying to purchase lived experiences. To ensure a profitable event, venues need to consider the overall consumer experience, not just the band lineup.</p>\n<p><strong>Text 2</strong></p>\n<p>Music festival appearances are becoming a more important part of musicians&rsquo; careers. One factor in this shift is the rising use of streaming services that allow access to huge numbers of songs for a monthly fee, subsequently reducing sales of full-length albums. With this shift in consumer behavior, musicians are increasingly dependent on revenue from live performances.</p>","stem":"<p>Based on the texts, both authors would most likely agree with which statement?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"886c4ccc-e592-4439-85aa-3a66dd54b114","content":"<p>Consumers are more interested in paying subscription fees to stream music than in attending music festivals in person.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"5281ca3a-d5d2-4a97-9f53-9409b4b563a8","content":"<p>Consumers&rsquo; growing interest in purchasing experiences is mostly confined to the music industry.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"0ac4657c-1962-4b2d-bfcd-d48fa72f2c5c","content":"<p>Changing consumer behaviors are leading to changes in music-related businesses.&nbsp;</p>"},{"id":"c385be7d-6a68-4af3-a2d9-a5578301fe83","content":"<p>The rising consumer demand for live music festivals also generates higher demand for music streaming platforms.</p>"}],"keys":["0ac4657c-1962-4b2d-bfcd-d48fa72f2c5c"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is the best answer. Both authors mention how consumer behaviors have shifted, and how this affects different aspects of the music industry. Text 1 states that consumers enjoy purchasing &ldquo;lived experiences,&rdquo; and that this influences how organizers design music festivals. Text 2 states that consumers are using streaming services more, and that this reduces album sales and increases the importance of live performances for musicians. </p><p>Choice A is incorrect. Neither text claims that consumers prefer streaming to festivals, or that these are mutually exclusive options. Text 1 implies that festivals are popular and profitable, and Text 2 never suggests that streaming services diminish the demand for live music. Choice B is incorrect. This choice misreads Text 1, which identifies music festivals as just one example of a broader trend of purchasing &ldquo;lived experiences.&rdquo; Text 2 doesn&rsquo;t mention growing interest in purchasing